   "bio": "James McGuire was born on 12 January 1861 at Bloomsburg, Columbia County, Pennsylvania. In 1870, aged nine, he was in the household of Edward McGuire, a furnace helper, in Mahoning Township, Montour County, where the post office was Danville; his son William later named Danville as James's birthplace.\n\nBy the 1880s James had moved to the coal towns of Plymouth and Larksville in Luzerne County, where he worked as a laborer, living at Plymouth in 1900 and at Larksville from 1910 to 1920. He married Anna C. Jones, who was born in England in 1865, and they had at least eleven children, among them Edward J. (born 1885), Mary, James J., Marguerite, Francis J. (born 1898), Vincent, Theresa, William B., Anna C. and Joseph. He died at Wilkes-Barre on 23 May 1927 and was buried at Larksville.",
