   "researchNotes": "James McGuire was born 12 Jan 1861 at Bloomsburg, Columbia Co. (FS GZQN-SCM). In 1870 he was 'James 9' in the household of Edward McGuire, furnace helper, in Mahoning Twp., Montour Co. (P.O. Danville). He moved to the Plymouth/Larksville coal towns by the 1880s; laborer; Plymouth 1900; Larksville 1910–20. He married Anna C. Jones (b. England 1865). They had 11+ children including Edward J. (1885), Mary, James J., Marguerite, Francis J. (1898), Vincent, Theresa, William B., Anna C. and Joseph. He died 23 May 1927 in Wilkes-Barre (PA death certificate attached to the FS profile).\n\nThe 1927 Pennsylvania death-certificate index lists \"McGuire, James; 54803; W-Barre; May 23\" ([R4-S1]), matching the FamilySearch death date. Six months later his son William Bernard's marriage application described James as dead and born at Danville, Pa. ([R4-S2]). Danville is the post office of Mahoning Township, Montour County, where Edward McGuire's household, including a son James aged 9, was enumerated in 1870 ([R4-S3]). That ties Kathryn's grandfather to the Danville furnace family by a record independent of the FamilySearch tree."
