   "summary": "English-born daughter of a Welsh miner who came to Plymouth, Pennsylvania, as a child and married James McGuire; John's 2nd-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Anna C. Jones was born in England in March 1865, the daughter of Edward F. Jones, a Welsh-born miner, and Margaret McIver, who was English. The family crossed to America in the 1870s, probably about 1870 to 1872, and by 1880 were living in Plymouth Township, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania; her sisters Rose and Mary had been born in England, while her brother William J. was born in Pennsylvania in September 1879.\n\nAnna married James McGuire and became the mother of at least eleven children, among them Francis J. McGuire, born in 1898. The families were doubly joined when her brother Joseph S. Jones married Agnes M. McAvoy, a sister of Anna's daughter-in-law Elizabeth. The McGuires lived at Plymouth in 1900 and at Larksville by 1910, and Anna died at Larksville on 2 January 1925 and was buried there. She is John's 2nd-great-grandmother.",
