   "occupation": "Miner (1880)",
   "bio": "Edward F. Jones was born in Wales about 1840, of Welsh parents, and worked as a miner. In June 1880 he was living in Plymouth Township, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, aged 40, with his wife Margret and their children Ann C., 15, Rose, 13, and Mary, 10, all born in England, and William J., born in Pennsylvania in September 1879. The children's English births show that he had worked in England, probably in a mining district, from at least 1865 until about 1870 before emigrating. Next door lived Evan W. Jones, 60, and Martha, 52, both Welsh and possibly kin.\n\nHe died in 1889 and was buried at Larksville, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania; when his son Joseph married in 1914 he was recorded as deceased and born in Wales. He is John's 3rd-great-grandfather.",
   "openQuestions": [
    "Children born in England c.1865-1870: a 1871 England census search (Ancestry/FindMyPast) for Edward & Margaret Jones with Ann, Rose and Mary would show where they lived."
   ],
