   "bio": "William Bernard McGuire was born on 17 September 1906 at Plymouth, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, or by another record at nearby Larksville, where he was living in 1910 and 1920. He was a son of James McGuire, born at Danville, Pennsylvania, and Anna Jones, born in England, both of whom had died by 1927, and he was an uncle of Kathryn McGuire.\n\nOn 25 November 1927, a 21-year-old laborer living in Wilkes-Barre, he applied to marry Mary Marguerite Prout of Lyndwood, Hanover Township. They were married the next day by Rev. D. W. McCarthy, the same priest who had married William F. Meier and Florence Pringle the year before. Marguerite died in 1934, and on 29 December 1939 William married Alice Theressa Brennan in Luzerne County. He died in September 1975 at Mountain Top, Fairview Township, and was buried at St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Township.",
   "link": {
    "confidence": "confirmed",
    "note": "Round 4 (unverified → confirmed): 1927 marriage application names parents James McGuire and Anna Jones."
   },
