   "bio": "Catherine E. Heffernan was the eldest child of Andrew H. Heffernan and Mary Connole, who had married at Plymouth, Pennsylvania, on 1 September 1868. She was born at Plymouth on 2 August 1870, although some accounts put her birth a year earlier, in August 1869. In 1880 she was living in her father's household. She married Addison F. Pringle at Plymouth on 29 June 1892, and they had eight children: Genevieve (1893), Joseph Vincent (1895), Mary E. (1898), Anna Theresa (1901), Florence (1904), John's great-grandmother, Helen (1906), Francis (1909) and Catherine (1912). In 1910 the family was living at Plymouth and Larksville.\n\nHer brothers and sisters were Thomas F., the postmaster and newspaper owner; Nora C.; Anna P. (Murphy); Mary, who became Sister Mary Antonia, IHM; Dr. Andrew J.; Josephine R. (Wagner); John Vincent; Maj. Leo Gerald; and George Paul. Catherine died at Wilkes-Barre, Luzerne County, on 23 April 1947. She was John's 2nd-great-grandmother.",
