   "researchNotes": "Died 1754 aged about 96. Justice of the peace and sheriff; member of the NY Assembly 1693–98; commissioner to lay out the King's Highway from Brooklyn to East Hampton (Akerly 1898). Married Mehitable Wells, daughter of William Wells by his second wife Mary — since Wells's first wife was Bridget, widow of Henry Tuthill (John Jr.'s grandmother), the couple were not blood relatives. Children (Akerly) include James (of Brookhaven and Orange Co.), Mary (1687–1780, m. Jonathan Horton; mother of Rev. Azariah Horton), Freegift (1698–1765), Joshua (m. Hannah Reeve) and John III of Southold (will 1740). Cousins through him and Mehitable: Rev. Azariah Horton (1C9R), Rev. Theodore L. Cuyler (5C5R).\n\nAkerly (1898) gives John Jr. b. 14 Feb 1658, d. 21 Nov 1754. He married Mehitable Wells (b. 1666, d. 26 Aug 1742) 'in or before 1683'. He was a Southold landowner, JP, commissioner for the King's Highway, NY Assembly member 1693-98, and sheriff ([R4-S1]). His children were John (b. 1683), James, Mary (1687, m. Jonathan Horton), Joshua (1690), Dorothy (c.1692, m. Joseph Brown), Daniel, Freegift (8 Aug 1698), and perhaps Hannah ([R4-S1]). The contemporary Salmon Record has the death of 'John Tuthil aged 96 years old' on the 21st in a November run of entries ([R4-S2]), matching Akerly."
