   "summary": "Daughter of Southold founder William Wells and wife of John Tuthill; John's 9th-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Mehitable Wells was born at Southold, Suffolk County, New York, in 1666, a daughter of William Wells, one of the founders of Southold, and his second wife Mary. Family tradition makes her mother Mary Youngs, but historians have rejected this; Mary's maiden name is unknown, and the tradition probably arose because a deed of gift she made in 1678 names her daughter Mary Youngs. After William's death Mary remarried Thomas Mapes Jr.\n\nMehitable married John Tuthill, and their sons James and Joshua, who were full brothers, carry the Wells descent down to John; through William Wells the family has its strongest claim to a Society of Colonial Wars ancestor. She died at Southold on 26 August 1742 and is listed among that year's deaths as the wife of John Tuthill. She is John's 9th-great-grandmother.",
