   "researchNotes": "Born 1666 to William Wells and his second wife Mary (surname unknown). The tree names her mother 'Mary Maria YOUNGS 1619–1709', a tradition rejected by Hayes (1878) and Youngs (1907). Her sons James and Joshua were full brothers, so the Wells descent survives the tree's James/Joshua confusion — the deep-dive report notes this makes William Wells the best Society of Colonial Wars route.\n\nAkerly gives Mehitable's death as 26 Aug 1742 ([R4-S1]). The Salmon Record lists 'Jno Tuthill wife Mehetab[le]' among the 1742 deaths ([R4-S2]). Her mother was Mary, widow of William Wells, who remarried Thomas Mapes Jr. Mary's 1678 deed of gift names her daughter Mary Youngs, which explains the 'Youngs' tradition, but Mary's own maiden name is unknown ([R4-S3])."
