   "bio": "John Tuthill was born on 16 July 1635, probably in England, though the Hingham records point to a birth there, and died at Southold, Suffolk Co., NY, on 12 October 1717. After his father's death his mother Bridget married William Wells, who became guardian of John and his sister Elizabeth. He became a landowner at Southold, and the births of his children were recorded in his family Bible and in the Southold town records.\n\nHe married first Deliverance King, daughter of William and Dorothy King, who was baptized at Salem in 1641 and died at Southold aged 49. On 28 May 1690 he married second Sarah, probably the widow of Thomas Young and a daughter of John Frost, who died on 8 November 1727. His children were John, born on 14 February 1658, who married Mehitable, the daughter of his stepfather William Wells; Elizabeth, born in 1661, who married William Wells Jr.; Henry, born in 1665; Hannah, born in 1667, who married Joshua Wells; Abigail (1670); Dorothy (1674); Deliverance (1677); Daniel (1679); Nathaniel, born in 1683, who died at Antigua in 1705; and, by his second wife, Mary, who died young. His son Henry, known as the Justice, married Bethia Horton, a granddaughter of William Wells, and was the great-great-grandfather of First Lady Anna Symmes Harrison. John Tuthill is John's 10th-great-grandfather.",
