   "researchNotes": "Southold landowner; his children's births are recorded in his family Bible (Akerly). WikiTree's 'born Tharston' is uncertain; Akerly says 'in England?', and the Hingham records point to a birth there. After his father's death his mother Bridget married William Wells, who became guardian of the Tuthill children; his son John Jr. later married Wells's daughter Mehitable. Henry Tuthill 'the Justice' (b. 1665), who married Bethia Horton, granddaughter of William Wells, and was great-great-grandfather of First Lady Anna Symmes Harrison, is placed in this family by the relationship math (Anna is 4C7R via Tuthill). Wife not named in project files; the deep-dive report mentions 'Tuthill, King and Wells relationships' and Round 3 'Browne/King' ancestors, which suggests a King wife somewhere in this branch (not specified).\n\nAkerly (1898) gives John's birth as 16 July 1635 ('in England?') and his death at Southold on 12 Oct 1717 ([R4-S1]). He married first Deliverance King, daughter of William and Dorothy (Hayne?) King, baptized at Salem 1641 ('1641:31:8'), who died at Southold aged 49. He married second, on 28 May 1690, Sarah, probably the widow of Thomas Young and daughter of John Frost, who died 8 Nov 1727. His children's births were recorded in his Bible and in Liber E of the Southold town records. The children were John (b. 14 Feb 1658), Elizabeth (1661, m. William Wells Jr.), Henry (1665), Hannah (1667, m. Joshua Wells), Abigail (1670), Dorothy (1674), Deliverance (1677), Daniel (1679), Nathaniel (1683, d. Antigua 1705), and by the second wife Mary (d. young) ([R4-S1]). He and his sister Elizabeth were wards of their stepfather William Wells."
