   "bio": "Mary, whose maiden name is unknown, is recorded as born in 1619 at Norwich in Norfolk, England. About 1654 she married William Wells of Southold on Long Island as his second wife, and after his death she married Thomas Mapes Jr. A family tradition made her a Youngs, a sister or daughter of the Rev. John Youngs of Southold, but the historian Hayes could find nothing to support it, and the Youngs family's own genealogy lists no such daughter.\n\nHer own deed of gift of 26 December 1678, made as 'Mary Mapes of Southold, the relect of William Wells and now wife to Thomas Mapes Junr', gave property to her son-in-law John Youngs and 'Mary Yongs his wife my daughter'. The Youngs connection therefore came through her daughter's marriage, not through her own birth. A Southold record of 1677 mentions her son William Wells being taught a trade. She was still living at the end of 1678.",
