   "researchNotes": "Southold's founding minister (William Wells was its leading founder after him). Wives per Youngs (1907): Joan Herrington, Joan (Harris) Palgrave, Mary (Warren) Gardner. Children: John, Thomas, Mary (m. Edward Petty), Rachel, Joseph, Benjamin, Christopher. His sister married William Browne of Salem. Not in the Rootsweb Youngs index as father of a Mary Wells. Col. John Youngs and the Oyster Bay Youngses are therefore not proven kin.\n\nYoungs Family (1907) prints the inscription on Rev. John Youngs's altar tomb: 'Mr Iohn Yongs Minister of the Word and First Setler of the Chvrch of Christ in Sovth Hovld ... Deceased the 24 of Febrvary ... 1671/2 and of His Age 74' ([R4-S1]). It gives his marriages as (1) Joan Herrington at Southwold, 25 July 1622 (license of 24 July 1622, bond by Mr. Christopher Yongs), (2) Joan (Harris), widow of Richard Palgrave, and (3) Mary (Warren), widow Gardner, who died at Southold in 1678. His children were John, Thomas, Mary (m. Edward Petty), Rachel, Joseph, Benjamin and Christopher. No daughter married William Wells ([R4-S1]). The deed of gift of Mary Mapes (formerly Wells), 1678, shows that the Youngs link to the Wells family came through Mary Wells's daughter Mary, who married a John Youngs ([R4-S2]). He is therefore not an ancestor on present evidence."
