   "summary": "Norfolk emigrant of 1637 who settled first at Hingham, Massachusetts, and then at Southold on Long Island; John's 11th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Henry Tuthill was baptized as Henrye Tutthill at St Mary's, Tharston, Norfolk, on 28 June 1612, and was five years old when his father died in 1618. In 1637 he and his wife, then of Saxlingham in Norfolk, sailed from Great Yarmouth in the Mary Anne, William Goose master, for New England.\n\nHe settled at Hingham, Massachusetts, where he had a house lot in 1637 (some accounts also credit him with a planting lot in 1635), was made a freeman in 1638 and served as constable in 1640. On 20 June 1644 he sold out and moved to Southold on Long Island. He died there before 15 December 1650, though some records give 1644. His widow Bridget married William Wells. A suggestion that William Tuttle of New Haven was his brother William, baptized at Tharston in 1609, has been disproven. He was John's 11th-great-grandfather.",
