   "bio": "Anna A. Higgins, known as Annie and sometimes recorded as Anna Agnes, was born on 2 October 1867 at New Philadelphia in Schuylkill County, Pennsylvania, to a father born in Ireland and a mother born in Pennsylvania. Her parents may have been William Higgins and Mary Ann Reilly, but that has not been confirmed, and the family had probably left New Philadelphia before 1890.\n\nShe was living in Hazleton when she married Henry J. Meier there on 1 March 1892, and she was John's 2nd-great-grandmother. The couple lived at Tamaqua in Schuylkill County between about 1903 and 1906 and then settled in Wilkes-Barre, on Mill Street in 1910 and on Barney Street in 1920 and 1940. By 1910 she had borne seven children, of whom six were living.\n\nAnna died at Wilkes-Barre on 6 October 1951, aged eighty-four, and was buried in St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Township.",
