   "summary": "Born at Elmira, New York, to Irish immigrants and mother of the Wilkes-Barre Heffernans; John's 3rd-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Mary Connole was born at Elmira, Chemung County, New York, on 3 November 1850. Her parents, Thomas Connole and Honora Dwyre, were \"natives of Ireland, who came to America in 1848, settling in the State of New York\". Her obituary says she came to the Wyoming Valley in 1865, but her sister Nora was born in Plymouth Twp in 1855, so the family most likely reached Plymouth, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, between about 1855 and 1860.\n\nAfter her mother's death her father married Anastasia (Boney) Heffernan, an aunt by marriage of Andrew H. Heffernan, and on 1 September 1868 Mary married Andrew at Plymouth. She bore eleven children, ten of whom were living in 1900, and became the mother of the Wilkes-Barre Heffernans. She was living in Wilkes-Barre by 1914 and died there on 1 May 1928. She was buried at St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Township, Luzerne County. She is John's 3rd-great-grandmother.",
