   "summary": "Master glazier and cabinetmaker, citizen of Munzingen in Baden, who died at 46; John's 4th great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Servatius Birkenmayer was born at Munzingen, near Freiburg im Breisgau in Baden, on 4 May 1807, the son of Johann Birkenmayer, an official in the service of the manor, and Magdalena Erb. His marriage record gives the year as 1807, while his age at death implies 1806; 1807 is the better supported. His May birth fits his name, since the feast of St. Servatius falls on 13 May.\n\nOn 17 October 1836, by then a master glazier and citizen of Munzingen, he married Maria Agatha Heizler, born there on 26 June 1813, the daughter of the late Joseph Heizler, a huntsman in the manor's service, and Maria Anna Federer. The witnesses were Josef Ott, a farmer, and Johann Federer, formerly a glazier and by then a farmer. Their children included Joseph, born at Munzingen on 15 March 1842, who died at Sandusky, Ohio, in 1904, and Maria Anna, John's ancestor. Servatius was recorded as a glazier in 1837, as a citizen and glazier in 1842, and at his death as master joiner, cabinetmaker and glazier.\n\nHe died at Munzingen on 19 April 1853, aged 46, having received the last sacraments, and was buried on 21 April; the witnesses were his brother-in-law Friedrich Heizler, the gravedigger, and Johann Schell, a teacher. His toddler son Heinrich died about three weeks later. Later parish entries of 1862 and 1867 still remembered him as 'the late citizen and joiner Servatius Birkenmaier'. His widow Agatha died in 1867.",
