   "summary": "Daughter of the Kageneck seigneurial gamekeeper at Munzingen in Baden (1813–1867), wife of the joiner Servatius Birkenmayer; John's 4th-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Maria Agatha Heizler, known as Agatha, was born on 26 June 1813 at Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, in Baden, the daughter of Joseph Heizler, the seigneurial gamekeeper of the Kageneck lordship, and M. Anna Federer of Munzingen; her father was dead by the time of her marriage. Her name repeats that of Agathe, the daughter of Jakob Heitzler born in 1771, which supports her probable descent from the gamekeepers of Ibental. On 17 October 1836 she married Servatius Birkenmayer, a citizen and joiner of Munzingen, and they had at least seven children between 1837 and 1852.\n\nShe was widowed on 19 April 1853, when her brother Friedrich Heitzler, born in 1809, served as gravedigger at her husband's burial, and she lost her son Heinrich only weeks later. She never remarried. She died at Munzingen at three in the morning on 3 August 1867, having received the last sacraments, aged 54 years, 1 month and 8 days, and was buried on 5 August; the witnesses were the gravedigger Johann Georg Birkenmaier and a farmer.\n\nFamily records had called her Maria Anna Heitzler, with the right birth year but the wrong first name. She was not the Maria Anna Heitzler born at Unteribental in 1813, daughter of the Ibental schoolteacher, nor a daughter of the Wehrlehof family of Joseph Heitzler and Maria Rombach; and the Agatha Heitzler of the Dreisamtal, born about 1810 to Andreas Heitzler and Agatha Schlegel, who had children at Stegen in the 1830s, was a different woman, probably a first cousin. She is John's 4th-great-grandmother.",
