   "bio": "Johann Evangelist Birkenmayer was born on 10 January 1771 at Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, Baden-Württemberg, Germany; family records name his parents as Matthias Birkenmayer (1739–1803) and Caecilia Hohler, born in 1752. He married Magdalena Erb, and their children included Servatius Birkenmayer. When Servatius married in 1836 the register described his father as \"herrschaftl. Waibel\", which, if the reading is right, means a bailiff or beadle in the service of the local lordship, and noted that Magdalena was already dead.\n\nHe died at Munzingen on 17 December 1844, a widower and day labourer aged 73 years and 11 months, and was buried on 20 December. He is not to be confused with a Johann Birkenmaier of Kirchzarten (1762–1847), husband of Gertrud Steinhart, who was a different man. Johann Evangelist was John's 5th-great-grandfather.",
