   "summary": "Wife of James Smith and a granddaughter of Capt. Elnathan Topping of Sagg, Southampton; John's 8th-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Jerusha Topping was born at Southampton, Suffolk County, New York, about 1698, though the accounts place her birth anywhere between 1695 and 1705. The best evidence makes her a daughter of Elnathan Topping Jr. (1664–1751) and his wife Mary, and so a granddaughter of Captain Elnathan and Mary (Cooper) Topping and a great-granddaughter of Thomas Topping. Her father's will of September 1751 left five shillings each to his daughters Phebe, Mary and Jerusha, a token sum consistent with a daughter already married; her brothers and sisters were Elnathan, Job, Silas, Luther, Zephaniah, Mary and Phebe. Some published genealogies instead give her parents as Josiah Topping and Hannah Sayre, or as Jonathan and Mary Topping, but neither version fits the 1751 will.\n\nAbout 1720 she married James Smith; their eldest son Matthew was born on 3 September 1721, and a daughter Temperance in the early 1730s. Jerusha died in 1760 at Long Island City, Queens. She was John's 8th-great-grandmother.",
