   "researchNotes": "Bull Smith had a son Adam, b. 1649; William Hammond's will (1662) left 'Adam Smith, son of daughter, Sarah' a mare colt and £20 'if he behave obediently to my wife'. The tree's 'Justice A Smith' card carries a Smithtown 350th logo image and pairs him with Elizabeth Thompson 1657–1718. Preferred: Job Smith is James's father; Adam is a collateral uncle.\n\nPelletreau prints Adam Smith's will of 12 June 1704, which leaves 'all estate to his only son Edmund Smith' (not probated) ([R4-S1]). The Introduction says 'Adam is said to have died in 1720' ([R4-S2]), against the tree's 2 July 1726. Adam therefore cannot be the father of James Smith of Moriches, and the tree's pairing of Adam with Elizabeth Thompson is wrong: she was Job's wife ([R4-S3])."
