   "bio": "Emma Aldridge was probably baptised about July 1611 at Langley Marish, a chapelry of Wraysbury in Buckinghamshire. Her father Ambrose bought the manor of Remingham and Cow in Wraysbury in 1611 and sold it for £500 two years later.\n\nShe married Capt. Thomas Topping, who married three times in all. The couple joined the Milford church in 1640, and their son Elnathan was baptised there on 2 August of that year. Since Thomas's next marriage contract is dated 20 October 1666, Emma was the mother of Capt. Elnathan Topping, the line through which she is John's 11th-great-grandmother. She died in 1665 at Southampton, Suffolk County, New York.",
