   "bio": "Frances Meier was born at Munzingen in Baden on 8 March 1863 and baptized two days later as Franziska Mayer, 'legitimate daughter of the local citizen and mason Friedrich Mayer and Maria Anna Birkenmaier, both Catholic'. She was the first child born after her parents' marriage in October 1862, and her godparents came from both sides of the family: her mother's brother Joseph Birkenmaier, then twenty, and her father's sister Paulina Mayer, then twenty-two. She was a sister of Henry J. Meier and John's 3rd-great-aunt.\n\nIn America she married Philip Miller and was known as Frances Miller. From 1900 the couple lived at Coal Dale in Rahn Township and then at Coaldale, Schuylkill County, Pennsylvania. She died at Coaldale on 10 December 1928 and was buried at St Joseph's RC Cemetery, Summit Hill.",
