   "summary": "John's 4th great-grandfather, a mason and later master mason of Munzingen in Baden, whose family lived in house No. 68.",
   "bio": "Heinrich Mayer was born about 1796 at Munzingen near Freiburg im Breisgau in Baden, the son of the Munzingen citizen and carpenter Michael Mayer. On 16 October 1820, aged 24 and already working as a mason, he married Juliana Senn, 22, at Munzingen; the register describes her as a parentless local citizen's daughter, born out of wedlock to a mother of the same name, and records that he was married 'with house No. 68'. The couple made their home in that house, which apparently came with the marriage. The witnesses were the citizens Heinrich Schmid and Heinrich Kuner, and the priest Flamm signed the record. The Latin form of his name, Henericus, explains why he was later remembered in America as 'Henery Meier'. The godparents of his first child in 1821 were the local masons Anton Mayer and Joseph Mayer, who may have been kin.\n\nHeinrich was a mason in 1820 and 1835 and had risen to master mason by 1862. In January 1862, when his son Friedrich acknowledged a grandson at a Munzingen baptism, the priest described Heinrich as a living citizen and master mason of the town; Heinrich's daughter Sophie, of age and unmarried, stood as godmother and was then in domestic service at Freiburg. He was still living in October 1862. Where and when he died is not known; he may have died away from Munzingen, perhaps at Freiburg, where his daughters Sophie and Pauline lived, or have emigrated.\n\nThe family name was written Mayer in the Munzingen registers through 1862. In America it appeared as Meyer in 1870 and Myer in 1880, and the spelling Meier first appears in the 1892 marriage record of his grandson Henry J. Meier, written by the clerk; from 1910 on Meier was the settled form, and no formal change of name was ever recorded. Heinrich was John's 4th great-grandfather.",
   "residences": [
    {
     "date": "1820",
     "place": "House No. 68, Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, Baden-Württemberg, Germany"
    }
   ],
