   "bio": "Thomas Connole, whose name was also written Connolly, was born in Ireland about 1815. Connole is a north Clare surname, found mainly in Clare, Galway and Cork, and one record places his birth in County Clare, though that is unproven. He and his wife Honora Dwyre were \"natives of Ireland, who came to America in 1848, settling in the State of New York\". Their children Mary, born in 1850, and John F., born 9 March 1853, were born at Elmira, and Honora, called Nora, was born in Plymouth Twp about 1855, by which time the family had moved to Luzerne County, Pennsylvania.\n\nIn Plymouth he kept a restaurant, which his son John F. briefly managed after his death. After Honora died, perhaps at Elmira, he married Anastasia (Boney) Heffernan, widow of Richard Heffernan; the marriage took place after 1860, when she was still recorded under the Heffernan name. He died in 1878 at Plymouth and was buried at St. Mary's, Hanover Twp. He is John's 4th-great-grandfather.",
