   "researchNotes": "John Scott Harrison (4 Oct 1804 - 25 May 1878) was a son of President William Henry Harrison and Anna Tuthill Symmes, born at Grouseland, Vincennes, and the father of President Benjamin Harrison; he is the only American who was both son and father of a president ([R4-S1]). He studied law but farmed at Point Farm, North Bend, Ohio, and served two terms in Congress (1853-57), first as a Whig and then as an Anti-Nebraska man. He married (1) Lucretia Knapp Johnson in 1824 (three children) and (2) on 12 Aug 1831 Elizabeth Ramsey Irwin (1810-1850), daughter of Archibald Irwin and Mary Ramsey, with whom he had ten children, including Benjamin ([R4-S1]).\n\nHe died suddenly at home in May 1878. The New York Herald of 31 May 1878 carried the Cincinnati telegraph story: the family had seen that a neighbour's grave had been robbed and took 'extraordinary precautions', yet the body was stolen; his son John and grandson George Eaton, searching the Ohio Medical College with a warrant for the other body, hauled up a corpse on a rope and recognised it ('My God, it's father!'). The scandal fed into Ohio's 1881 anatomy law ([R4-S2], [R4-S1])."
