   "researchNotes": "Kin only through his Long Island grandmother Anna Symmes, not through the Virginia Harrisons of Berkeley Plantation. William Henry Harrison and John Tyler are related by marriage only; Theodore Roosevelt is not kin. Harrison extension cousins (John Scott Harrison; William Henry Harrison III of Wyoming) were not researched.\n\nPath verified: John Tuthill (1635) -> Henry (1665) -> Henry (1690) -> Henry (d. 1793) -> Anna Tuthill -> Anna Symmes Harrison -> John Scott Harrison -> Benjamin, 7 generations: 6th cousin 5 times removed (Akerly [R4-S2]; Wikipedia [R4-S1] for the Harrison generations). Second route via William Wells (Bethia Wells -> Bethia Horton -> Henry 1690 ...), 8 generations: 7th cousin 4 times removed. Conditional third route via Barnabas Horton (7C5R, twice) if the Rachel Browne line holds. His Virginia Harrison ancestry is not John's."
