   "summary": "Seigneurial gamekeeper of the Counts of Kageneck at Munzingen in Baden, probably a son of the Ibental gamekeeper Jakob Heitzler; John's 5th great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Joseph Heizler was the herrschaftlicher Jäger, the seigneurial gamekeeper, of the Counts of Kageneck, who were lords of Munzingen, where their Schloss dates from 1672, and from 1702 of Stegen and the Ibental. He was born about 1773 at Weiler, Freiburg, Baden-Württemberg, Germany, and was probably a son of Jakob Heitzler, the Kagenecks' gamekeeper in the Ibental, and Catharina Begelspacher. Jakob's recorded children leave gaps that would fit a son born about 1773, and a gamekeeper's son serving the same lords at their Munzingen seat makes good sense, but the link is not proven. He was not the Ibental schoolteacher Joseph Heitzler (1765–1828), nor the Joseph of the Wehrlehof, and the family records, which give him the dates 1773–1825, may have run two Josephs together.\n\nOn 26 December 1799 he married M. Anna Federer of Munzingen there. Their children included Friedrich, born 8 March 1809, Agatha, born 26 June 1813, and Veronica, who died of measles on 29 April 1815 aged about a year and a half. He was therefore alive and living at Munzingen in 1815, and he had died by 7 October 1835, when he was described as the former seigneurial gamekeeper. He is John's 5th great-grandfather.",
