   "summary": "Maria Anna Federer of Munzingen, wife of the gamekeeper Joseph Heizler and mother of Agatha Heizler; John's 5th-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Maria Anna Federer was born in 1772 at Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, Baden-Württemberg, Germany, into the Federer family of that village; family records name her parents as Georgius G Federer (1732–1802) and Maria Anna Kaltenbach (1745–1808). She was not, as was once supposed, of the Fürderer farming family of Ibental. In 1799, described as \"von hier\", of this place, she married the gamekeeper Joseph Heizler. Their children included Friedrich, born in 1809, Agatha, born in 1813, and Veronica, who was buried in 1815.\n\nA Johann Federer, a former glazier turned farmer, witnessed Veronica's burial in 1815 and the 1836 marriage of Servatius Birkenmayer, and was probably her brother or her father; it may have been from him that Servatius learned the glazier's trade, though that is only a guess. Anna was still living when her son Friedrich married in 1835. She died at Munzingen on 13 May 1844. She was John's 5th-great-grandmother.",
