   "summary": "Gamekeeper and forest warden for the Counts of Kageneck at Unteribental in the Black Forest; probably John's 6th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Jacob Heitzler, or Jakob, was born about 1740 at Kirchzarten in the Breisgau. He served the Counts of Kageneck as gamekeeper and forest warden at Unteribental, and he figured in a lawsuit in 1789. His wife was Katharina Begelspacher, whose father had also been a Kageneck gamekeeper.\n\nTheir recorded children, born between 1764 and 1781, were Andreas (born 1764, who was Vogt of Unteribental in 1813), Agathe (1771), Franziska (1779) and Jakob (1781–1847); gaps in the record leave room for Joseph, born about 1773, through whom Jacob is probably John's 6th-great-grandfather. His parents are given as Martin Heitzler and Othilia Schirk, though the dates recorded for them do not fit well with his own birth. He died in 1806.",
