   "summary": "Guardia Lombardi-born wife of the Scranton grocer John Petriello and mother of James Petriello; John's maternal 2nd-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Maria Antonia DiBiasi, known in America as Marie or Mary, was born about 1870 at Guardia Lombardi, Avellino, Campania, Italy. Her parents are recorded as Giovanni P. DiBiasi, born in 1829, and Rosa Siconolfi, born in 1840, and her probable brother was Domenico Antonio DiBiasi, born at Guardia in 1856, who died at Scranton in 1922. She came to the United States in 1880, though one later record gives 1892, and married John Petriello, the Scranton grocer. In 1910 she was the mother of six children, all living, among them John's great-grandfather James; her married name was usually written Petrillo. The family lived on Ash Street in Scranton in 1910 and by 1920 at the family house and store on Bunker Hill Street.\n\nShe died at Scranton on 5 July 1935. A widowed Vincenzo DiBiasi, born in Italy about 1866, lived three doors from the Petriello house on Bunker Hill Street in 1940 and may have been her brother or cousin, and a Francesco De Biasi, aged 72, was the informant at the death of her father-in-law Pietro Petriello in 1901; neither connection is proven. She was John's maternal 2nd-great-grandmother.",
