   "bio": "Mary Young, also recorded as Maria Jung and Mary Croup, was born in Pennsylvania between 1770 and 1780; one account gives January 1776. She is said to have been the eldest child of Johannes Jung (John Young Sr.) of Easton, who died before September 1787, and Anna Maria Doll (1751-1813), a link that rests on her widowed mother's 1813 will. Her siblings were Sara, Johannes, Susannah, Peter, Catherine, Elizabeth, Henry, Jacob and Margaretha Young.\n\nShe married Frederick Croup, also written Grub, and the Shupp family genealogy independently calls their daughter Susan Croup Shupp \"daughter of Frederick and Mary (Young) Croup\". In 1840 a woman in her sixties, matching Mary, was living with Frederick in Plymouth Township. She is said to have died in Pennsylvania in 1841, though one account gives 3 September 1842. She is John's 5th-great-grandmother.",
