   "researchNotes": "Mary (Maria Jung) Young married Frederick Croup/Grub; Harvey's Shupp genealogy calls Susan Croup Shupp 'daughter of Frederick and Mary (Young) Croup', independently confirming the couple shown in John's tree. She is said to have died in 1841 (tree '-1841'); no record found. Her parents per the tree are John Young Sr. and Anna Maria Doll, a link with no online record.\n\nThe FamilySearch tree gives Maria (Young) Croup a birth in January 1776 and a death on 3 September 1842, and makes her the eldest child of Johannes Jung of Easton (d. before 12 September 1787) and Anna Maria Doll (1751-1813). Its only attached source is 'last will of Maria Young, Northampton Co PA, Will Book 4, p.458' ([R4-S1]) - evidently the 1813 will of her widowed mother, which would be the first document to tie Mary Croup to the Young-Doll family. The tree lists her siblings as Sara (1777), Johannes (1781-1813), Susannah (1783), Peter (1784-1854), Catherine, Elizabeth, Henry, Jacob and Margaretha Young ([R4-S1]). In 1840 a woman in her sixties was living with Frederick Croup in Plymouth Township, matching her ([R4-S2])."
