   "bio": "Anna Maria Doll was born on 16 May 1751 in Northampton County, Pennsylvania, in Plainfield Township according to family records. She married Johannes Jung, known as John Young Sr., who died before 1787, and they had ten children; the eldest, Maria, born in January 1776, married Frederick Grub, or Croup, and is John's ancestor. Anna Maria died on 29 June 1813 in Pennsylvania, and her will, made as Maria Young, was proved in Northampton County.\n\nFamily records make her a daughter of Johann Caspar Doll, called Captain, and Anna Margaretha Dietz, with brothers and sisters George (1744–83), Hannah (1746–73), Casper Dull (1748–1829), Sarah Margaretha (1748–79), Abraham (1752), Elizabeth Margaret (1754–88) and Anna Catharina (1757–99). The connection is probable but unproven: no record names her parents, and Casper Doll's known daughters are Hannah, Elizabeth, who married Christopher Stecher, and Anna Catharine. The Stechers also married into the Grubs, so these Forks Township families were closely intertwined. She was John's 6th-great-grandmother.",
