   "summary": "Wife of Johann Casper Doll, buried at Plainfield, Northampton County, Pennsylvania, in 1790; John's 7th-great-grandmother.",
   "bio": "Anna Margaretha Dietz, known as Margaret, was the wife of Johann Casper Doll. Family records give her birth as 15 February 1724 at Rieschweiler in Zweibrücken, though this is not documented; several Dietz families from Eschweiler and Rieschweiler in Zweibrücken did settle in Plainfield Township, Northampton County, Pennsylvania, where the Dolls lived. Her parents are possibly Johann Adam Dietz Sr. (1696–1769) and Anna Catharine Abel (1704–1753), who are said to have died in the Wind Gap and Plainfield area, but that identification is only a candidate. She was recorded as 'Margaret' at the Tohickon Reformed Church in 1757 when her daughter Anna Catharine was baptized. She died in Plainfield Township on 23 April 1790 and was buried in Plainfield Cemetery, where she has a gravestone. She is John's 7th-great-grandmother.",
