   "bio": "Daniel Scott is said to have been born in 1778 at Woodford, Bennington, Vermont, a son of Matthew Scott of Bennington, who died in 1789, and to have died at Pittstown in Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, in 1811. Family trees name him and his wife Hannah Devens, born in 1787, as the parents of Stephen J. Scott, but the claim is unproven.\n\nWhat the records do show is that a 'Daniel Scott Jr.' headed a household in Pittston Township in 1810 made up of a man aged between 26 and 44, a woman between 16 and 25 and three young children, two of them boys, which fits a man born in 1778 with a young wife. The 'Jr.' suggests an older Daniel Scott in the same area, and one appears among the taxpayers of neighbouring Providence Township in 1796. A Joseph Scott and a young Stephen Scott were listed on the same census page. All of this is consistent with, but does not prove, the claim that Daniel was Stephen's father. If he was, he is John's 5th-great-grandfather.",
