   "summary": "Contadino of Guardia Lombardi, husband of Grazia Di Marino and father of John Petriello; John's 3rd-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Pietro Petriello, also written Petrillo, was born about 1837 at Guardia Lombardi, Avellino, Campania, Italy, a son of Angelo Petriello and Lucia Marra; a son's 1869 birth record, giving his age as 33, points to about 1836, and his death record to about 1837. He was a contadino, a peasant farm labourer. His sister Gaetana married Giuseppantonio Lucadamo in 1855.\n\nHe married Grazia Di Marino, born about 1845, the daughter of Gaetano di Marino and Caterina di Leo, probably between 1863 and 1868; an indexed Avellino civil record naming the couple together with her parents is very likely their marriage act. Their children included John Petriello, John's 2nd-great-grandfather, and Filomena, born in the neighbouring town of Carife on 16 December 1885, which places the family there that year.\n\nPietro died at his home on Via Piazza in Guardia Lombardi on 29 March 1901, aged 64, described as a contadino born in Guardia and the husband of Grazia Di Marino. The death was reported by Francesco De Biasi, aged 72, a sign of how close the Petriello and Di Biase families were.",
