   "researchNotes": "Tree: Pietro Petrillo/Petriello + Grazia Di Marino (b. 1837). Son's 1869 birth act: Pietro Petriello fu Angelo, 33, contadino (so born c.1836). Death act: died 29 Mar 1901, Guardia (Via Piazza), aged 64 (so born c.1837), contadino, born in Guardia; son of the late Angelo and the late Lucia Marra; 'marito di Di Marino Grazia'; Morti 1901 act 28; the declarant was Francesco De Biasi, 72 (showing the families were close). Round 2 had this as probable from the FS tree (sourced to Avellino civil registers, FS records 6PG6-674L and 6PG6-674V). The FS tree also gives him an impossible wife 'Grazia Sasso, 1796-1848' - ignore. His sister Gaetana Petriello married Giuseppantonio Lucadamo in 1855. The marriage of Pietro and Grazia was not found: Guardia marriage indexes for 1855-61, 1863, 1865 (part) and 1866-68 were checked; 1862 and 1864 registers are not on Antenati. Grazia was born c.1845, so the marriage was probably c.1863-68 (1862, 1864 or a missed page of 1865).\n\nThree FamilySearch-indexed Avellino civil records are attached to Pietro's tree profile ([R4-S1]). The first (ark 1:1:6PG6-674L) indexes Pietro together with Grazia di Marino (6PG6-674V) and her parents Gaetano di Marino (6PG6-674K) and Caterina di Leo (6PG6-6742), all under one record. That pattern is typical of a marriage act, so it is very likely the Petriello–Di Marino marriage that Round 3 could not find in the Antenati indexes. The second (6PJX-KPGJ, with Angelo Petriello, Lucia Marra and Grazia) is his 1901 death act, already read. The third is the 16 Dec 1885 birth of daughter Filomena at Carife (QPR6-CHPY), which places Pietro and Grazia in neighbouring Carife in 1885. The images are blocked from here, so the record date of 6PG6-674L is unknown."
