   "bio": "Giovanni Pasquale Dibiasi, whose surname is also written Di Biase, was born about 1829 at Guardia Lombardi, Avellino, Campania, Italy, a son of Domenico Di Biase (born 1789) and Angela Carrozzino. He married Rosa Siconolfi, born about 1839 or 1840, and their children Domenico Antonio (born 1856) and Maria Antonia (born 1870), John's 2nd-great-grandmother, were born at Guardia. A claim that the couple were born at Lucera in Foggia province is probably a confusion with another family of the same common surname.\n\nTwo younger children sometimes attributed to them, Joseph (born 1891) and Vincenzo, known as James (born 1894), cannot be theirs, since Rosa would then have been in her fifties. In 1940 Joseph and James DiBiasi were living as neighbours on Bunker Hill Street, a few doors from the Petriello house, and close by lived a widowed Vincenzo DiBiasi, aged about 74, with his son Michael. That Vincenzo is a more plausible father for the two, and may himself have been a younger son of Giovanni Pasquale and a brother of Maria Antonia.",
