   "bio": "Grazia Di Marino was born about 1845 at Guardia Lombardi, Avellino, Campania, the daughter of Gaetano di Marino (1795-1876) and Caterina di Leo. Some family records give her birth as 1837 and her mother as Maria d'Ambrosio, but her death record settles both points; Maria d'Ambrosio was probably Gaetano's earlier wife, the mother of Concetta di Marino, who married in 1855. Grazia's probable full sister Maria di Marino, also a daughter of Gaetano and Caterina di Leo, married Nicola di Pietro on 12 February 1857. The di Leo surname is that of Fr. Nunzio Di Leo, whose will funded Guardia's St. Rocco chapel after the plague of 1656.\n\nGrazia married Pietro Petriello and was the mother of John Petriello. A daughter Filomena, born on 16 December 1885 at Carife, is also attributed to her, which would have made her a mother at about 40. A contadina, she died at Guardia Lombardi on 9 May 1916, aged 71, the widow of Pietro Petriello. She is John's maternal 3rd-great-grandmother.",
