   "bio": "Gaetano di Marino was born about 1796 at Guardia Lombardi, Avellino, in Campania, a son of Pietro di Marino and Felicita Magnotta. He was a contadino, or farmer, and died at Guardia in March 1876, aged eighty, the death record calling him the husband of Caterina di Leo. He was John's maternal 4th-great-grandfather.\n\nHe probably married twice. His first wife, Maria d'Ambrosio, was the mother of Concetta, who married Giuseppe Petriello on 26 December 1855. His second wife, Caterina di Leo, was the mother of John's ancestor Grazia and probably of Maria di Marino, who was born about 1835, married on 12 February 1857 a Nicola di Pietro, or di Paola as another record has it, and died at Guardia on 29 December 1914. If Maria's birth year is right, Gaetano had married Caterina by about 1834, which would place his marriage to Maria d'Ambrosio before then; otherwise the 1835 date may be wrong. Some family trees have run the two wives together by making Maria d'Ambrosio the mother of Grazia.",
   "facts": [
    {
     "label": "Tree display (IMG_7830-7840)",
     "value": "Gaetano di Marino 1795-1876"
    }
   ],
