   "summary": "Day-labourer's son of San Mango d'Aquino who married Saveria Colosimo and raised seven children there; John's maternal 3rd-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Domenico Gabriele Fiorillo was born at San Mango d'Aquino in Catanzaro, Calabria, on 27 December 1840, the son of Carmine Fiorillo, a 32-year-old bracciale or day-labourer, and Giuseppina Ferlaino; a Gaetano Colosimo witnessed the registration of his birth. The Fiorillos were newcomers to San Mango, having arrived in the town during the 1800s, and every documented Fiorillo who left Calabria for the United States came from there.\n\nOn 1 April 1870, his father having already died, Domenico, styled Gabriele in the register, married Saveria Colosimo, daughter of Raffaele, in the San Mango parish. Seven children were baptized between 1871 and 1886: Giuseppina, John's ancestor, in 1871, then Carmelo (1873), Filomena (1874), Carolina (1877), Carmine (1880), Antonio (1884) and Gaetano (1886), who married Maria Mendicino in 1909. Domenico never emigrated. The parish burial register records him, aged 81 and the son of the late Carmine and the late Giuseppa Ferlaino, buried at San Mango on 27 August 1921, though family records give his death as 1927. He is John's maternal 3rd-great-grandfather.",
