   "researchNotes": "Tree: Saveria Colosimo (1848-1926). Colosimo is one of the commonest San Mango surnames: 652 entries in the 1674-1804 parish stati delle anime; Colosimo x14 in the mid-1990s San Mango phone directory; listed by ItalianSide among the town's traditional families. A Gaetano Colosimo, 40, witnessed Domenico Fiorillo's 1840 birth act (relationship unknown).\n\nSaveria was baptized on 26 October 1848, daughter of Raffaele Colosimo and Filippina Iera ([R4-S1]). The tree's 25 October is probably her birth date. She married Domenico Gabriele Fiorillo at San Mango on 1 April 1870 ([R4-S2]). The parish burial index has Saveria Colosimo, widow of Domenico Fiorillo, buried 10 August 1931 with a stated age of 70 ([R4-S3]). Husband and widowhood match (Domenico died 1921), but the age is about twelve years too low. This entry is a candidate for her death and conflicts with the tree's 26 May 1926."
