   "summary": "Day labourer of San Mango d'Aquino, born at Savuto, who married Giuseppina Ferlaino in 1840; John's maternal 4th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Carmine Gabriele Fiorillo was born about 1808 at Savuto in the province of Cosenza, Calabria, the son of Domenico Fiorillo and Maria Marrelli, whose surname is also written Marrello and Morrello. He had ties to Aiello Calabro: two of his sisters, Cintia (Giacinta) and Antonia, were born there and married at San Mango d'Aquino in 1839 and 1844. On 1 March 1840, aged 34 and described as a contadino from Savuto, Carmine married Giuseppina Ferlaino in the civil ceremony at San Mango d'Aquino; the church wedding followed two days later, and the parish entry notes that the groom came from Aiello. Both his parents were still living at the time of his marriage; his mother was buried in 1846.\n\nHe worked as a bracciale, a day labourer, and was so described at the birth of his son Domenico on 27 December 1840. He died at San Mango d'Aquino on 17 November 1860, aged about 52. His death record named his mother as Vittoria Marrelli, but Vittoria was in fact the wife of Francesco Gabriele Fiorillo, very probably Domenico's brother, and the informant evidently confused the two women: Maria, not Vittoria, was Carmine's mother. He is John's maternal 4th-great-grandfather.",
