   "summary": "Domenico Gabriele Fiorillo, born at Cannovali near Aiello Calabro and died at San Mango in 1849, father of Carmine Fiorillo; John's 5th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Domenico Gabriele Fiorillo was born at Cannovali, a hamlet of Aiello Calabro in the province of Cosenza, about 1775, the son of Carmine Gabriele Fiorillo and Giacinta, known as 'Cintia'; the records differ on his mother's surname, giving it as Feraculo or Iera. A probable brother, Francesco Gabriele Fiorillo, died in 1853. Some accounts give Domenico's birth year as 1785, but his age at death points to about 1775.\n\nThe Fiorillos were Aiello people who moved down the Savuto valley to San Mango d'Aquino in the early 1800s, which is why no Fiorillo appears in San Mango's parish lists before 1804; the pedigree sometimes given for the family before Domenico is unsupported. His wife, Maria Marrello, died in 1846, although their son Carmine's death record calls her Vittoria. Domenico died at San Mango on 6 June 1849 and was buried the next day. He was the father of John's ancestor Carmine Fiorillo.",
