   "bio": "Maria Marrello, whose name is also written Morrello and Marrelli, was born in 1786 at Aiello Calabro, Cosenza, Calabria, the daughter of Vincenzo Marrello and Giacinta Gabriele Fiorillo. She married Domenico Gabriele Fiorillo; their daughters Cintia and Antonia were born at Aiello Calabro, and their son Carmine named her, still living, as his mother at his marriage in 1840. She was buried at San Mango d'Aquino on 20 March 1846, aged 60.\n\nCarmine's death record instead calls his mother Vittoria Marrelli, so the records disagree, but the marriage record names Maria directly and she is most likely Carmine's mother, and so a direct ancestor of John. The family records that give her mother as Ippolita Guercio and trace a longer pedigree above her are unsupported.",
