   "bio": "Matthew Scott was born at Sunderland, Massachusetts, on 4 August 1739, or 21 August by another account, and died at Kingsbury in Washington County, New York, on 22 January 1813. Records credit him with a long run of Vermont militia service from 1764 to 1782, including Revolutionary War rolls for the years 1778 to 1782, and place him at Bennington, Vermont, in the 1790 census; if confirmed, that service would make him a second Revolutionary patriot in John's ancestry.\n\nHe is shown as John's 6th-great-grandfather through a son, Daniel Scott, born in 1788, and Daniel's son Stephen J. Scott, born in 1806. Neither link is documented, and the Daniel Scott Jr. found at Pittston in 1810 was too old to be the Daniel born in 1788, so Matthew's connection to John remains unverified.",
