   "bio": "Edward McGuire was born in Ireland about 1824. He may have been the Edward baptized on 7 April 1824 at St. Mary's, Haddington Road, in Dublin, a son of Owen McGuire and Anne Clusky, with a sister Margaret baptized in January 1819, but nothing beyond the name and year ties that baptism to him. He had settled in Pennsylvania by about 1856, when his eldest child was born there.\n\nIn 1870 he was living in Mahoning Township, Montour County, near Danville, and working as a furnace helper in the iron works; Danville was the home of the Montour Iron Works, whose rolling mill is credited with the first T-rails made in America, in 1845. With him were his wife Mary Jane and their children Edward, 14, Mary, 12, James, 9, Marcella, 5, and Timothy, 3, all born in Pennsylvania. His son James gave Danville as his birthplace. Mary (1858-1942) became Mrs. Michael E. Riley of Plymouth; Cecilia Marcella (1864-1918) married Murdock Dunn at Plymouth in 1887 and emigrated to Vancouver Island, British Columbia; Timothy, born about 1865, had died by 1880.\n\nEdward McGuire died at Plymouth, Luzerne County, on 4 April 1907 and was buried there. He is probably John's 3rd-great-grandfather.",
