   "bio": "Henry James Meier, known as Harry, was born on 24 August 1894 in Hazleton, Pennsylvania, and was a brother of William F. Meier. At 15 he was an apprentice saddler in a harness shop. On 13 June 1917, by then a 22-year-old moulder like his father, he married Mary M. Proudlove of Forty Fort, the daughter of an English-born blacksmith.\n\nIn January 1920, listed as 'Harry J. Jr.', he was working as a labourer at an iron works and living on Barney Street in Wilkes-Barre, next door to his parents, with his wife Mary and their small son Robert. The family was still on Barney Street in 1930 and 1940, and he lived there to the end of his life. His children were Robert J. (1918–1998), Marjorie (1920–2010), who married Harold Stitzer, Harry J. Jr. (1924–1995) and Regina (1926–2012), who married Francis Gimber.\n\nHe died in Wilkes-Barre on 29 January 1957, aged 62, and was buried on 1 February in St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Township. He is John's 2nd great-uncle.",
