   "summary": "Glazier's son from Munzingen in Baden who emigrated to Sandusky, Ohio; John's 4th great-uncle.",
   "bio": "Joseph Birkenmayer, later also spelled Birkenmeier, was born on 15 March 1842 at Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, Baden-Württemberg, Germany, and baptized there four days later, the legitimate son of Servatius Birkenmayer, a citizen and glazier of Munzingen, and Agatha Heizler; the farmer Gabriel Ott and the teacher Johann Schell stood as witnesses. He was a brother of Maria Anna Birkenmayer, and is John's 4th great-uncle.\n\nHe was still at home in March 1863, working as a day labourer. When his sister Maria Anna's second child, Franziska, later Frances Meier Miller, was baptized on 10 March 1863, he was her godfather, described as the twenty-year-old single son of the late Servaz Birkenmaier, and he signed the register as a witness. Some time after that he left for America, following the well-worn path from Munzingen to northern Ohio. He died at Sandusky, Erie County, Ohio, on 3 November 1904.",
