   "summary": "Munzingen-born gardener who stayed with the Meiers in Hazleton in 1880 and settled in Sandusky, Ohio; brother of Maria Anna and John's 4th great-uncle.",
   "bio": "Gabriel E. Birkenmeier was born at Munzingen, near Freiburg in Baden, on 20 January 1849, a brother of Maria Anna Birkenmaier, the wife of Friedrich Mayer. In June 1880 he was living with his sister's family in Hazleton, Pennsylvania, a 29-year-old gardener who was laid up on census day with \"fever & ague\", a malaria-type fever; that census entry, which lists him as Friedrich's brother-in-law, is the record that confirms Maria Anna's maiden name.\n\nHe later moved to Sandusky, Ohio, where his brother Joseph lived. There he married Caroline C. Kratz, an Ohio-born woman from Venice in Erie County, and they had at least four children. His eldest son, Frank Birkmaier, a machinist, died at Providence Hospital in Sandusky on 4 April 1930, aged 45, and his daughter Rhea married Charles W. Prentice in Michigan. Gabriel died at Sandusky on 2 December 1896 and was buried at St. Mary's Cemetery there. He is John's 4th great-uncle.",
