   "bio": "Karolina Birkenmayer was born at Munzingen near Freiburg im Breisgau in Baden about 21 January 1846, the daughter of the joiner Servaz Birkenmaier and Agatha Heitzler, and a sister of Maria Anna Birkenmayer; she was John's 4th great-aunt. She worked as a seamstress. When her sister Maria Anna's family left for America in 1868, Karolina stayed behind in Munzingen.\n\nShe died there, unmarried, at one in the morning on 16 March 1869, aged 23 years, 1 month and 25 days, both her parents having died before her, and was buried on the 18th. The witnesses at her burial were the gravedigger Johann Georg Birkenmaier and the single mason Johann Birkenmaier, both probably kin. With her death, only her brothers Joseph and Gabriel, both in Ohio, and Maria Anna in Pennsylvania were left of the family.",
