   "bio": "Friedrich Heitzler was born at Munzingen, Freiburg im Breisgau, Baden-Württemberg, Germany, on 8 March 1809, the son of Josef Heizler, the lordship's gamekeeper, and Anna Federer, and a brother of Agatha Heizler. On 7 October 1835, at Munzingen, a single day labourer of 26 whose father was already dead, he married Francisca Widlebacher, who was born on 28 September 1811. By 1853 he was the village gravedigger, and in that capacity he witnessed the burial of his brother-in-law Servatius Birkenmayer.\n\nFriedrich died far from Munzingen, at five in the evening of 15 December 1865, in a place read as Brombach in the Wiese valley near Lörrach, though an earlier reading of the name was Lörrach itself. The Protestant parish there informed the Catholic parish of Munzingen of the death of \"Friedrich Heitzler, Bürger von Munzingen\", and the Catholic vicar buried him on 18 December. His age was recorded as 56 years, 9 months and 7 days, which matches his birth exactly. Why a Munzingen day labourer and former gravedigger was in the Lörrach district is unknown; he may have been working on the railway or in the textile mills of the Wiesental.",
