   "bio": "Anna Meier, also recorded as Annie or Maria Meier, lived in Wilkes-Barre, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania. She was a depositor at the bank of F. V. Rockafellow on its last day and lost $700 when it failed. She then pursued the embezzlement case against Rockafellow from 1893 to 1897, carrying it to the Superior Court, which in 1897 reversed a lower-court ruling; she told the judge in open court that she \"did not think justice had been done\". She died in July 1897 after a fall on her way home from visiting friends on Grove Street.\n\nShe was not John's ancestor Maria A. Meier, and whether she was related to the family at all is unproven.",
