   "bio": "Maria Elisabetha Christmann was born on 9 August 1729 at Kollweiler, in the Reichenbach Lutheran parish, the daughter of Jacob Christmann and his wife Anna Margaretha, and was baptized on the 14th, the ninth Sunday after Trinity; her godparents included a Conrad of Nanzweiler and a Maria Elisabetha. Some family records give her mother's maiden name as Raab and her parents' marriage as 24 November 1722 at Kollweiler, but the surname is unverified. On 19 September 1752 she married Johann Andreas Grub at Jettenbach, and in 1754 she emigrated with him to Pennsylvania.\n\nWidowed in 1792, she served as co-executor of her husband's estate with their son Frederick, and later married the widower Christopher Bittenbender. Her own will of 1810 names \"her son Frederick Krub\". She died on 19 January 1815 at Easton, Northampton County, Pennsylvania, and was buried in Easton Cemetery. She was John's 6th-great-grandmother.",
