   "summary": "Church elder of Jettenbach in the Palatinate, baptized at Berschweiler in 1655; John's 8th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Johann Peter Grub was baptized on 28 February 1655 at Berschweiler bei Kirn, Birkenfeld, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany. In the generations after the Thirty Years' War his family moved from Oberbrombach to Berschweiler and then to Jettenbach, where from 1700 he served as Kirchenzensor, or church elder. He died at Jettenbach on 15 October 1739.\n\nHe married twice. His first wife, Gretha Catharina, also written Margretha Catharina, stood with him at the baptisms of their daughters Anna Catharina in August 1684 and Margretha Catharina in 1687 in the Reichenbach Lutheran parish; her children were born between 1679 and 1694, the last being Johann Nickel, and she died before October 1694. On 19 October 1694, at Glan-Münchweiler, he married Elisabetha Catharina Jung (about 1674–1734), daughter of Paul Jung, and had at least eight more children with her. Some family records run the two wives together as a single \"Gretha Catharina Jung\". He was John's 8th-great-grandfather.",
