   "researchNotes": "Baptized 28 Feb 1655 at Berschweiler; married 19 Oct 1694 at Glan-Münchweiler; Kirchenzensor (church elder) at Jettenbach from 1700; died at Jettenbach 15 Oct 1739. The family moved from Oberbrombach to Berschweiler to Jettenbach in the generations after the Thirty Years' War.\n\nJohann Peter Grub married twice. The Reichenbach register shows him with a wife Gretha Catharina at the baptism of his daughter Anna Catharina in Aug 1684, and with Margretha Catharina at a daughter's baptism in 1687 ([R4-S1], [R4-S2]). FamilySearch gives that first wife's death as before Oct 1694 and has her children born from 1679 to 1694, ending with Johann Nickel. On 19 Oct 1694 at Glan-Münchweiler he married Elisabetha Catharina Jung (c.1674-1734), daughter of Paul Jung, and had at least eight more children ([R4-S3]). The 1694 marriage is the date the site gives for him, but the site attaches it to a single wife, 'Gretha Catharina Jung', which merges the two women (see H0078)."
