   "bio": "Gretha (Margretha) Catharina was the first wife of Johann Peter Grub and is named as the mother at the baptisms of their daughters in the Reichenbach Lutheran parish in 1684 and 1687; her maiden name is unknown, and she had died by October 1694. On 19 October 1694 Peter married Elisabetha Catharina Jung (about 1674-1734), daughter of Paul Jung of Jettenbach and Maria Barbara, and it was she who died at Jettenbach on 28 March 1734. The family records combine the two women under the single name Gretha Catharina Jung. The Grubs of Jettenbach married into the Jung family for generations.\n\nWhich wife was the mother of Johann Nickel Grub, born about 1694, decides whether John descends from this Jung marriage: if Nickel was born before October 1694, John's 8th-great-grandmother is the first wife, whose surname is unknown. Either way the Jungs are among John's ancestors through Maria Sara Jung, mother of Elisabetha Margaretha Lampert.",
