   "researchNotes": "Abraham Lampert was the smith (Schmied) of Jettenbach, father of Elisabetha Margaretha (b. 1702).\n\nHis daughter's baptism on 17 Dec 1702 names him as 'Abraham Lamperti' of Jettenbach, with his wife Maria Sara ([R4-S1]). FamilySearch gives him a birth of about 1676 at Otterberg, a marriage at Glan-Münchweiler on 6 Oct 1699 to Maria Sara Jung (widow of Johann Philipp Wirth), and his death at Jettenbach on 18 Jun 1711. It names four children: Maria Elisabeta (1700-1706), Elisabetha Margaretha (1702), Maria Catharina Barbara (1706-1767) and Johann Peter (1708-1713). It also names his parents as Jacob Lampert and Margaretha ([R4-S2]). An Otterberg origin would fit the Walloon/Reformed settlement there, but it is unsourced."
