   "summary": "Of Erzweiler in Ulmet parish, husband of Sara Schuch and father of Johann Casper Doll; John's 8th-great-grandfather if the Doll link holds.",
   "bio": "Christoffel Doll was born on 6 July 1671 at Erzweiler, in the parish of Ulmet in the Kusel district, and was baptized at Ulmet three days later, the son of Hans Peter Doll of Erzweiler (1647–1717) and Gertraud Fick. On 2 March 1704, in the Lutheran church at Ulmet, he married Sara, daughter of Johann Peter Schuch, whose home village is read, with some uncertainty, as Ratsweiler. They had twelve children between 1705 and 1729, among them Maria Engel (1717–1784), who married Jacob Sorber in 1739, and Johann Casper, born in 1722, who is John's ancestor.\n\nEarlier Dolls of Erzweiler, Abraham Doll, who died there in 1651, Peter Doll (about 1611–1688) and Elisabetha Margaretha Doll, baptized at Ulmet in 1652, may have been of the same family, though their link to Christoffel has not been shown. Family records say that Christoffel died in 1739 on the ship Samuel while crossing the Atlantic, which would explain why only his younger relatives qualified at Philadelphia; the 'Stoffel Doll, aged 40' on that ship's list was a younger man, perhaps a son or nephew. The death at sea is not documented. He is John's 8th-great-grandfather if the Doll link holds.",
