   "summary": "Of the Schuch family of Ulmet, mother of Johann Casper Doll, who ended her days in Bucks County; John's 8th-great-grandmother if the Doll line holds.",
   "bio": "Anna Sara Schuch, more probably called Sara or Sara Margaretha, was born on 11 January 1686 at Rathsweiler in the parish of Ulmet and baptized on 28 March, a daughter of Hans Peter Schuch (1661-1747) and Anna Maria Käppel. On 2 March 1704 she was married at Ulmet, the register calling her Sara, daughter of Joh. Peter Schuch. She was the mother of Johann Casper Doll and, if the Doll connection holds, John's 8th-great-grandmother.\n\nShe appears to have followed her son to Pennsylvania. Her Schuch kin apparently sailed with Casper in 1739, among them 'Christ. Shook, 48' on the ship Samuel, and a Johann Christian Jacob Schuch, born at Ulmet on 4 May 1690, died in Springfield Township, Bucks County, in 1768. Women were not listed on those ships, so she herself would have gone unrecorded. She is said to have died at Tohickon, Bucks County, on 3 April 1760 and to have been buried at Bedminster the next day as 'Sarah Doll', which would place her near the Tohickon Reformed congregation where her granddaughter Anna Catharina was baptized in 1757.",
