   "bio": "Paul Jung lived at Jettenbach, where he was born about 1640 and died before 1707. He and his wife Maria Barbara had nine children, born between 1660 and 1687. Among them were Elisabetha Catharina, about 1674 to 1734, who became the second wife of Johann Peter Grub, and Maria Sara, born about 1678 and dead before 1721, who married Abraham Lampert.\n\nJohn's descent from Paul Jung runs most securely through Maria Sara, the mother of Elisabetha Margaretha Lampert, though the evidence is not complete: Maria Sara's place as Paul's daughter rests on baptism entries, and her own daughter's baptism names her only as Maria Sara. He is John's 9th-great-grandfather.",
