   "summary": "Born at Oberbrombach, he married Elisabetha Birgert at Lauterecken in 1642 and died at Berschweiler in 1671; John's 9th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Caspar Grub was born at Oberbrombach, Birkenfeld, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany, and baptized at Niederbrombach on 26 May 1616, a son of Christmann Grub; his mother is given as Elssa in some records and Margaretha in others. On 9 January 1642 at Lauterecken he married Elisabetha Birgert of Fockenberg-Limbach, daughter of Conrad Birgert.\n\nHe settled at Berschweiler, where he was described as an inhabitant of the village. He died there early on the morning of 30 April 1671 and was buried on Monday 1 May with a funeral sermon, the Lutheran register recording his age as 53 years, 11 months and 3 days. That age would put his birth a year later than his baptism, but such ages were often a year out. Some records give his death as 29 April.",
