   "summary": "Christmann Grub of Oberbrombach in the Birkenfeld district, father of Caspar Grub; speculatively John's 10th-great-grandfather.",
   "bio": "Christmann Grub lived at Oberbrombach in the Birkenfeld district. The records give his birth as either 1576 or 1596 and his death as about 1633. His parents are given as Hanns Grub (born 1560) and Elsa, who died in 1597. Family records name his wife as Margaretha, though another account calls her Elssa and gives her birth as 11 April 1597; an Elsa appearing both as Hanns's wife dying in 1597 and as Christmann's wife born in 1597 looks like a muddle.\n\nHis children were Veltes (born 1615) and Caspar (born 1616), and the record of Caspar Grueb's marriage to Elisabetha Birkhert in 1642 names Christmann as the groom's father. The descent from him is speculative, but if it holds he is John's 10th-great-grandfather and his parents are John's 11th-great-grandparents.",
