   "bio": "Pierre Masse was a Huguenot refugee who, with his wife Elisabet Mercereau, had reached New York by the spring of 1689. His origin was probably Moëze in Saintonge, and he seems to have fled France together with his wife's Mersereau kin; the date usually given for his marriage, 29 April 1681, and the Daniel Masse of Moëze sometimes named as his father both rest on tradition rather than record.\n\nThree children were baptized at the French Church in New York: Daniel, born 29 April 1689 and baptized on 5 May, with Daniel Mercereau as godfather and Marie Pare, wife of Ezéchiel Grazilier, as godmother; Pierre, baptized 25 June 1693, with Jean La Tourette and Marie Suzanne Doucinet as godparents; and Jeanne, born 22 May and baptized 5 July 1696. Pierre witnessed all three Mersereau weddings of July and August 1693, and an Elie Masse who signed beside him that year was probably a brother. He himself stood godfather to several children in the 1690s.\n\nHis son Daniel married Ester Fourret and had Pierre (1712), Jean (1716) and Ester (1718) baptized at the same church, with his sister Jeanne as godmother to the youngest. Jeanne Masse married Daniel Lamoureux, and an Ester Masse was godmother to their son Andre in 1722; these sponsorships tie Jeanne, John's ancestor, firmly to Pierre's family. No burial for Pierre appears in the church register. He is John's 9th-great-grandfather.",
