   "bio": "William Davenport of Fordham Manor and West Farms, Westchester, appears in the records from 1680 to 1718, together with his wife Mary. One county historian wrote that \"William Davenport and his wife Mary came from England in 1670\", while the family genealogists think he came as a boy; both are guesses. The family genealogy proposes as his parents a John Davenport and his wife Mary of Long Neck, near New Rochelle, said to have come to America in 1670 with four children, but calls that first generation a supposition; its only document is a deed of January 1682/3 in which John and Mary sold land on Long Neck. The story of coming from England in 1670 is thus told of John and Mary in one place and of William and Mary in another. His English origin is unknown, and suggested connections with the Davenports of Bramhall in Cheshire and with the Rev. John Davenport are unsupported or disproven.\n\nAccording to the family Bible, as copied in the Davenport genealogy, his children were Thomas (1682–1759), William (1683–1735), Francis (1685–1720) and Rachel, though these may not have been all of them. The Bible was given to a grandson in 1759 and its entries are copies, so it is family evidence rather than a contemporary record. William was John's 9th-great-grandfather.",
