   "tags": [],
   "summary": "Newtown, Connecticut, man who married Anar Turner in 1759 and may have been the father of Samuel Pringle; a possible 6th-great-grandfather of John.",
   "bio": "James Prindle was born on 5 August 1736 at Newtown in Fairfield County, Connecticut. On 22 January 1759 he married Anar Turner, \"both of Newtown\", in the Newtown church. He died at Newtown on 9 December 1800, though some accounts give 9 November.\n\nHe is a possible rather than proven ancestor. Children assigned to him and Anar are James (about 1754), David (1757), Benjamin (1764), a militia private, Samuel (about 1767) and Hannah (1773), the same set of siblings found later in Orange County, New York. The first two were born before the 1759 marriage and could only be his by an unrecorded earlier wife, or belong to someone else. If Samuel was his son, James is John's 6th-great-grandfather, but that link is not yet documented.",
