   "bio": "Hannah Turner, recorded as \"Anar Turner\", married James Prindle of Newtown, Connecticut, on 22 January 1759, according to the Newtown church register. She has been identified as Hannah Turner, a daughter of Samuel Turner (1713-1794) and Rebeckah Cheesebrough, born at New London on 7 September 1738, who is said to have died on 19 July 1838 aged 99 and to have been buried at Stonington.\n\nThat identification is doubtful. The same Turner family also had a daughter Anna born in 1740, and \"Anar\" is a closer spelling of Anna or Anner than of Hannah; her birth records are indexed under both names, and the death and burial of a Newtown man's widow at Stonington at the age of 99 are not supported by any source. The children attributed to the marriage include James \"Pringle\" (1754-1828) and David (born 1757), who were born before the 1759 wedding and so cannot be hers unless the marriage date is wrong, as well as Benjamin (1764), Samuel (about 1767), John's ancestor, and Hannah (1773). She is a possible 6th-great-grandmother of John, no more.",
   "sources": [
    "The Prindle Genealogy (1906) p.41",
    "[R4-S1] Newtown, Conn., church register, marriage of James Prindle and Anar Turner, 22 Jan 1759 (FS Connecticut Church Records ark 1:1:QGR1-ZV95) (primary) https://ancestors.familysearch.org/service/tree/tree-data/published/sources/L8MP-W4X/images/i/2/image.jpg",
    "[R4-S2] FamilySearch published tree, Hannah Turner (L8MP-W4C): parents Samuel Turner & Rebeckah Cheesebrough; b. 7 Sep 1738 New London; d. 19 Jul 1838; children; citing CT Births and Christenings (arks 1:1:F7W9-MG9 'Anner Turner', 1:1:F7WM-5FQ) (derivative) https://www.familysearch.org/service/tree/tree-data/published/persons/L8MP-W4C",
    "[R4-S3] Prindle, Franklin C., The Prindle Genealogy (1906), p.41: James b. 5 Aug 1736, m. Newtown 22 Jan 1759 Anar Turner, d. Newtown 9 Nov 1800 (secondary) https://archive.org/stream/prindlegenealogy00prin/prindlegenealogy00prin_djvu.txt"
   ],
