   "summary": "Wilkes-Barre dentist for more than fifty years who built the Heffernan Building; John's 2nd-great-grand-uncle.",
   "bio": "Dr. Andrew Joseph Heffernan was born on 27 February 1881, a son of Andrew H. Heffernan, an Irish-born clerk, and Mary Connole, who was born in New York. At nineteen, in 1900, he was working as a wire maker. He attended Wyoming Seminary and took his dental degree at the Philadelphia Dental College, now part of Temple University, in 1907. He was John's 2nd-great-grand-uncle.\n\nHe practiced dentistry in Wilkes-Barre for more than fifty years, built the Heffernan Building there, served as president of the Susquehanna Dental Society and State Grand Master of Psi Omega, and sat for nineteen years on the state dental board. In Philadelphia in November 1914 he married Lillian T. MacDonald, daughter of a director of the Corn Exchange National Bank. He was still living in Wilkes-Barre in 1940, died on 17 November 1959 and was buried at St. Mary's Cemetery, Hanover Township.",
