   "summary": "Nurse trained at Reading who moved to California with her husband George Wagner and lived to 100; John's 2nd-great-grand-aunt.",
   "bio": "Josephine R. Heffernan was born on 30 December 1883. She trained as a nurse, graduating from St. Joseph's Hospital at Reading in 1906, and married George Julius Wagner, a Californian born on 27 January 1876. The couple settled in California, where they had two daughters, Josephine Eugenia (1909–1976) and Mary Georgia (1911–2008).\n\nGeorge died in 1927, leaving Josephine a widow at about 43. She lived another 57 years, in Piedmont, Berkeley and Oakland, and died at Alameda, California, on 8 March 1984, aged 100. She rests in the Chapel of the Chimes Columbarium and Mausoleum at Oakland.",
