   "summary": "Tipperary widow who brought her Heffernan children to Plymouth, Pennsylvania, and became stepmother to Mary Connole; aunt by marriage of John's ancestor Andrew H. Heffernan.",
   "bio": "Anastasia Boney, known as Anty, was born in County Tipperary, Ireland, about 1812. On 12 February 1827 she married Richard Heffernan, baptized in 1806, at Gortnahoe, and the couple lived at Mardyke. Richard died in Ireland, and Anastasia emigrated with her children to Plymouth, Pennsylvania. In 1860 she was living there with her son James and a 30-year-old Jeremiah Boney, probably a relative. After 1860 she became the second wife of the widower Thomas Connole, which made her stepmother to Mary Connole, the wife of Andrew H. Heffernan.\n\nShe died at Plymouth on 3 August 1896, aged 84. Her obituary recorded that she had married twice, that her first husband had died in Ireland, that her children were James Heffernan and Katherine Heffernan Grimes, and that her stepchildren were Mrs. Andrew Heffernan, John F. Connole and Mrs. William Dalley. Her surviving children were Catherine (1833–1908), who married Edmund Grimes; John (1835–1891), who married Margaret Fennelly; and James (1838–1910), who married Ellen Kelly.\n\nAs the widow of Richard Heffernan, brother of Andrew's father Thomas, she was Andrew H. Heffernan's aunt by marriage as well as the stepmother of his wife. It has been suggested that she and Andrew's mother Catherine Boney were sisters who married two Heffernan brothers, which would make her his blood aunt too, but that is unproven.",
   "sources": [
    "Find a Grave 162159301: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=162159301",
    "Find a Grave 183145812 (John F. Connole obituary): https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/183145812/john_francis-connole",
    "Michael Dwyer, Heffernans of Slieveardagh (Welsh Hill Press, 2020), Branch 4 (and Branch 3), working from the Killenaule and Gortnahoe Catholic parish registers: https://archive.org/details/heffernans-of-slieveardagh",
    "1860 Plymouth census"
   ],
