   "summary": "Surgeon who practised in Plymouth for fifteen years and then in Wilkes-Barre from 1923; John's 1st cousin 4 times removed.",
   "bio": "Dr. John P. Connole, also known as John Francis Connole Jr., was born at Plymouth, Pennsylvania, on 25 November 1882, a son of John F. Connole and Mary E. Keating. He became a surgeon and practised in Plymouth for fifteen years before moving his practice to Wilkes-Barre in 1923. He married Catherine Buckley in Luzerne County on 29 June 1911. When he registered for the draft in September 1918 he was a doctor of medicine living on Church Street in Plymouth; by 1930 he was living in Wilkes-Barre.\n\nHe died at Wilkes-Barre on 29 August 1945 and was buried at St. Mary's Cemetery in Hanover Township. He was John's 1st cousin 4 times removed.",
