   "bio": "Benjamin Pringle was born on 24 January 1794, one of the five sons of Samuel and Martha Pringle; his death and burial record of 1853 names his parents as Sam and Martha Pringle. He married Charity Gould, born in 1800, a granddaughter of Thomas and Charity (Lamoreaux) Davenport. In 1840 he headed a household of about ten in Plymouth Twp, a few doors from Samuel and James Pringle.\n\nTheir children were Bethia, who married Caleb Roberts in 1852 and went to Iowa; Martha Ann, who married William Hutchinson; Lege, born in 1825; Ira, born in 1833; Jacob Gould, who married first a VanScoy and in 1864 the widow Ellen C. (Fuller) Nesbitt; Martin, who went to California; and Caleb, born in 1839, who \"went West\". Benjamin died on 6 January 1853 and was buried at Larksville, Luzerne Co., PA. He is John's 4th-great-grand-uncle.",
