   "bio": "Caleb Atherton Pringle was born in Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, in June 1839, a son of Benjamin Pringle and Charity Gould, and was probably John's 1st cousin 5 times removed. He was living in Salem Township in 1860 when the Civil War came, and on 4 November 1861 he enlisted as a private in Company G of the 52nd Pennsylvania Infantry, known as the \"Luzerne Regiment\", serving until he was discharged at the end of his term on 5 November 1864.\n\nThe family history records that he \"went West\". He was still in Salem Township in 1870, but by 1880 he was in Rockford Township, Floyd County, Iowa, in 1885 in Clay County, Iowa, and he also lived for a time at Sanborn in O'Brien County, where he belonged to the Grand Army of the Republic. By 1900 he had settled at Rolla, Missouri, where he was still living in 1910. He died at Rolla on 22 April 1919 and was buried in Rolla Cemetery.",
