   "summary": "Samuel Pringle the younger of Plymouth Township, husband of Huldah Ives and father of Orange, Ransom and Keturah; probably John's 4th-great-grand-uncle.",
   "bio": "Samuel Pringle was very probably a son of Samuel and Martha Pringle, and so probably John's 4th-great-grand-uncle. His wife Hulda Ives (1804-1886), whom he married at Plymouth in 1824, gave their children the names Orange, Ransom and Keturah, names that belonged to the Lamoreaux family, which is the main reason for placing him in this family. He was living in Plymouth Township in 1830 and 1840; the 1840 census shows him as a man between thirty and forty with a wife in the same age bracket and nine children, next door to James Pringle and two doors from Joseph Ives. One record gives his birth year as 1794, but his age in 1840 suggests he was born between 1800 and 1810. He is said to have died on 25 March 1847, the same date recorded for his father, so one of the two dates may have been copied from the other. He was buried at Shawnee Cemetery.",
