   "bio": "Orange Pringle was born on 7 February 1827 in Plymouth Twp., Luzerne Co., PA, the son of Samuel D. Pringle and Hulda Ives. In 1850 he was a 23-year-old teamster living with his widowed mother. He married Elizabeth Ann Keller (1835–1912), and their children were Samuel, born at Plymouth on 26 November 1852, Emma Ann, born at Plymouth on 22 October 1854, Lenora (1857–1872) and Adelia, born at Dunkirk, Wisconsin, in 1873.\n\nBetween 1857 and 1870 the family moved west to Dane County, Wisconsin, living first at Albion and then at Dunkirk. Their son Samuel died at Edgerton in 1882 and Emma Ann in 1928; Orange also appears as a parent in a Wisconsin marriage record of a Miles Herrick, probably a daughter's marriage. He died in Rock County on 26 June 1900 and was buried in Fassett Cemetery, Edgerton. He is probably John's 1st cousin 5 times removed.",
