   "bio": "Noah Pringle was born at Plymouth, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, on 16 February 1834, the son of James and Elizabeth (Croup) Pringle and grandson of Samuel and Martha (Lamoreaux) Pringle. By 1850 he was already working as a farmer at sixteen. On 15 November 1857 he married Esther Louisa Nesbitt, and they had six children; a son, Frank E. Pringle, later died in Ohio. Noah lived at Plymouth throughout the years from 1850 to 1880 and died at Beach Haven, Luzerne County, on 28 April 1885. Esther afterwards lived at Ives, Dundee Co., Nebraska. He was a brother of John's ancestor Andrew G. Pringle, whose parentage his own well-recorded family establishes, and so John's 3rd-great-grand-uncle.",
