   "researchNotes": "David Pringle (Prindle), b. 1757 per FamilySearch, married Susannah Lamoreux in 1783 in Orange Co.; a David Prindle was a private, 1st Regt Orange Co. militia.\n\nThe officiating minister's own journal spells the name Prindle and dates the marriage 3 Sep 1783. Giles & Franklin give 22 July 1783, which in Constant's list is the date of the preceding couple, Francis Gale and Elizabeth Lewis. So 22 July is a misreading, and 3 Sep is the correct date ([R4-S1], [R4-S2]). The journal's editor thought David was 'probably of the Waterbury [Conn.] family of that name' ([R4-S1]). Giles & Franklin say he is also given as 'Pringle-Miller', and list three daughters: Elizabeth (m. Miles Davenport), Minerva (m. ___ Underwood) and Frances (m. Freeman Polk) ([R4-S2])."
