   "summary": "Sister of Ensign Thomas Lamoreux who, with her husband Thomas Davenport, founded Plymouth's Davenport clan; John's 6th-great-grand-aunt.",
   "bio": "Charity Lamoreux was born on 26 January 1759 and baptized at Philipstown, New York, on 27 March 1760, a sister of Ensign Thomas Lamoreux and John's 6th-great-grand-aunt. Her baptism at Philipstown confirms her family's connection with that place. On 22 February 1774, at Newburgh in Orange County, she married her first cousin Thomas Davenport (1749-1812), and in 1794 the couple came to Plymouth, Pennsylvania, where they founded the Davenport clan; their sons became known as the \"Davenport congress\".\n\nTheir daughters married into the Pringle family: Phoebe married John Pringle, and Hannah married Jacob Gould and became the mother of Charity Gould Pringle. Charity was still living as a widow in 1820 and died on 4 October 1848.",
