   "bio": "Stephen Davenport was born at Plymouth, Luzerne Co., PA, on 14 August 1800, the youngest child of Thomas and Charity (Lamoreux) Davenport. He served as a Luzerne County Commissioner and was remembered as the last of the \"Davenport congress\". In later life he lived in Huntington Township.\n\nOn 5 May 1822 he married Elizabeth Tubbs, who was born on 5 May 1802 and died on 24 March 1862. Their children were Hanford, who married Fanny Larned and died in 1865; William, born in 1827, who married Adaline Harrison in 1855; Thomas M., born in 1829, who married Diana Good; Earl; Samuel; and Charity Adelaide, born at Town Line, Pa., in February 1839, who married Charles Good and died at Hicks Ferry on 9 September 1930. Stephen died on 22 August 1882.",
