   "bio": "Phoebe Davenport was born on 4 May 1799, the daughter of Thomas Davenport and Charity Lamoreux, and was John's 1st cousin seven times removed. She married John Pringle and had nine children: Thomas (born 1821), Dennison (born 1830), Clara, who married Sam Shaffer and lived to ninety-four, Charity (born 1832), who married Andrew Worthington in 1855, William, Betsy, who never married, Lydia, Martha, who married a Weaver, and Stephen.\n\nIn 1850 the family was living in Plymouth Township, Luzerne County, with Thomas, Clarissa, Elizabeth, Lydia, William, Denison, Charity and Martha still at home. By 1860 Phoebe was a widow of sixty-two keeping house at Plymouth with her unmarried daughters Elizabeth and Lydia. Her will was recorded at Plymouth in 1867.",
