   "researchNotes": "Phoebe Davenport (1799 - after 1873) married John Pringle; nine children (see John Pringle). Will: Plymouth, 1867, vol. D p.344.\n\nGiles & Franklin give Phoebe's birth as 4 May 1799, daughter of Thomas and Charity (Lamoreux) Davenport, and say she married John Pringle (H0155). Their nine children: Thomas (b. 1821), Dennison (b. 1830), Clara (m. Sam Shaffer; d. aged 94), Charity (b. 1832; m. 1855 Andrew Worthington), William, Betsy (d. unmarried), Lydia, Martha (m. ___ Weaver) and Stephen ([R4-S1]). The censuses agree. In 1850 she was 52, in John's household with Thomas, Clarissa, Elizabeth, Lydia, William, Denison, Charity and Martha. In 1860 she was a 62-year-old widow keeping house with the unmarried Elizabeth (Betsy) and Lydia ([R4-S2]). Her will was proved in 1867."
