   "bio": "John Lamoreux was born at Monroe in Orange County, New York, on 5 March 1754, a son of Jean Lamoreaux and a brother of Ensign Thomas Lamoreaux, which makes him John's 7th-great-grand-uncle. During the Revolution he served in the New York militia and was captured when Fort Montgomery fell in October 1777.\n\nOn 9 June 1779 he married Jemima Stephens at Goshen. In the censuses of 1790 and 1800 he was listed as John Lamoreux Junior, with a separate household from his father. He died on 7 January 1823.",
