   "bio": "Andrew Losee Lamoreaux was born in 1812, a son of John McCord Lamoreaux and a grandson of Joshua Lamoureux, the youngest son of Daniel Lamoureux. Joshua, born in 1739, married Elizabeth Ogden, born in 1738, in Dutchess County; a Loyalist, he lived for a time in New Brunswick and then settled near Scarborough, York County, Upper Canada, close to Toronto. The Utah branch of the family descends from Joshua through Andrew and David Burlock Lamoreaux, who, as a family history of 1919 put it, \"went to that territory with Brigham Young\".\n\nAndrew became president of the French Mission of the Latter-day Saints. He died of cholera at St. Louis, Missouri, in 1855 while bringing converts west, so he never reached Utah himself; the family history, which calls him \"Andrew Lacy\", was speaking loosely when it said he went there with Brigham Young.",
