     "description": "Came from Northampton Co. with 'the numerous family of Sorbers'. Located on a 200-acre lot 'back of the mountain and up the creek' where Hiram Croop's mills were later built, and 'brought [it] to some degree of subjection'. His son William was born in Newport Twp. about 1805. [R4-S1]"
