   "researchNotes": "William Croop (1805-1889), lumberman; held township offices.\n\nBradsby says William, son of John Croop, was born in Newport Twp. and began his working life in Union (now Hunlock) Twp. There he married Mary Sorber, a native of Northampton Co. He was an extensive lumberman and farmer, owned 250 acres and a sawmill he had bought, held several township offices, and died in 1889 aged 84. Of his seven children, six were living in 1893, and Hiram (b. 15 Jul 1832) was the eldest. Andrew (b. 5 Aug 1843) was another ([R4-S1]). Bradsby names three sons who served in the Civil War: Alvin, Andrew and Simon."
