   "summary": "Hunlock Creek lumberman who ran four mills and served 25 years as justice of the peace; probably John's 3rd cousin 4 times removed.",
   "bio": "Hiram Croop was born on 15 July 1832 in Union (now Hunlock) Twp., Luzerne Co., PA, the eldest of the seven children of William Croop and Mary Sorber, and so a grandson of both John Croop and Philip Sorber. In 1854 he married Susanna Dodson, daughter of Joseph B. and Martha Dodson.\n\nHe became a lumberman on a large scale, at one time running four mills and owning 2,000 acres of timber, with a store at Croop's mills. By 1893 he owned farms of 180 and 125 acres in Hunlock Twp. and had served as justice of the peace for twenty-five years. In October 1883 he stood surety of $4,000 for Franklin Monroe, who was accused of shooting a tramp at Hunlock Creek. He is probably John's 3rd cousin 4 times removed.",
