   "researchNotes": "Dr. Harry Ward Croop (b. 1884), Wilkes-Barre physician; Stanley C. Croop is associated with the Croop's Glen amusement park at Hunlock Creek.\n\nHarvey & Smith's history (vol. V, 1929) has a sketch of Dr. Harry Ward Croop. He was born 16 Sep 1884 in Hunlock Township, son of Benjamin F. Croop (b. Hunlock Twp. 1856/58), owner and manager of the Croop's Glen amusement park at Hunlock's Creek, and Alvaretta Jane Eves (b. Columbia Co. 1858/59). He taught school for seven years, graduated from Jefferson Medical College in 1917, and served two and a half years as a Navy medical officer in World War I. After an internship at Wilkes-Barre General Hospital he practised at Kingston, stayed on the General Hospital staff, and was a Mason (Keystone Consistory, Irem Temple), Elk, Legionnaire and member of the Church of Christ, Kingston ([R4-S1]).\n\nThe same volume's sketch of his brother Stanley Carson Croop (b. 9 Mar 1897) says their father turned a hotel business into Croop's Glen, a picnic and amusement resort with pony rides and novelties, and that Stanley served 18 months on Submarine Chaser No. 62 in 1918-19 and was postmaster and storekeeper at Hunlock Creek from 1924 ([R4-S1]). Hiram Croop's surviving children in 1893 were Martha, Joseph H. and Fredrick W. (Bradsby p.812), so Benjamin F. was not Hiram's son. Harry Ward's exact descent from the pioneer John or Frederick Croop is still not traced."
