   "tags": [],
   "summary": "Maria Engel Doll of Ulmet, wife of Jacob Sorber and grandmother of Elizabeth Sorber Croop; possibly a sister of Johann Casper Doll.",
   "bio": "Maria Engel Doll was born on 15 September 1717 at Ulmet, Kusel, in the Rhineland-Palatinate, and died in 1785. In 1739, the year the Doll immigrants reached Pennsylvania, she married Jacob Sorber. Their son Abraham Sorber, born in 1744, moved from Northampton to Hanover Twp in Luzerne County, and his daughter Elizabeth Sorber married John Croop.\n\nShe may have been a sister of Johann Casper Doll, who arrived at Philadelphia on the Samuel in August 1739, aged 18, with Stoffel Doll (40) and Philip Doll (27), but her parentage is unproven. If she was, the Sorbers and Croops who built the sawmills on Hunlock's Creek were already cousins. Her husband's origin is also uncertain: a Sorber party that arrived at Philadelphia on the ship Elizabeth in August 1733 included several men named Jacob Sorber (spelled Surber and Server as well), a Rudolff Sorber, and the women Fronegh and Barbara Sorver, but the name is too common to say whether one of those Jacobs was Maria Engel's husband.",
   "sources": [
    "GEDBAS 1435014144: https://gedbas.genealogy.net/person/show/1435014144",
    "Plumb 1885 part 38",
    "[R4-S1] Strassburger & Hinke, Pennsylvania German Pioneers, vol. 1 (1934), Lists 30 A-C, ship Elizabeth, qualified 27 Aug 1733 (primary) https://archive.org/details/pennsylvaniagerm42stra"
   ],
