   "bio": "Rachel Browne married James Tuthill about 1714. Published genealogies give her parents as Jonathan Browne (1653–1710) and Elisabeth Salmon of Southold; Elisabeth was a daughter of William Salmon, who died in 1657, and Sarah Horton, daughter of Barnabas Horton of Southold, who was born at Mowsley in Leicestershire. Jonathan Browne is said to have died at Orient on 19 August 1710, though the Salmon Record enters a Jonathan Brown's death on 18 September of what appears to be 1704, and the two may or may not be the same man. She has sometimes been confused with Hannah Reeve, who was in fact the wife of Joshua Tuthill.\n\nHer children with James Tuthill were Rachel (1715), James (1717), Elizabeth (1719), Daniel (1721), Mary (1725), Jonathan (born 6 October 1727), Mehitable (1728/9) and John (1730). Among them were Daniel of Goshen and James Jr. of New Windsor, whose wills fit the family. Rachel is said to have died in 1738, though this is unconfirmed.",
