   "researchNotes": "Married James Tuthill about 1714. Not in the Ancestry tree, which instead shows 'Hannah S Reeve' as James's wife (an error merging Joshua Tuthill's marriage). WikiTree gives her parents as Jonathan Browne (1653–1710) & Elisabeth Salmon of Southold; Elisabeth was daughter of William Salmon (d. 1657) and Sarah Horton, daughter of Barnabas Horton of Southold, born Mowsley, Leicestershire. Brown executors in two Tuthill branches fit the marriage.\n\nWikiTree's profile quotes Alva Tuttle (1968, p. 279) for Rachel's children with James Tuthill: Rachel (1715), James (1717), Elizabeth (1719), Daniel (1721), Mary (1725), Jonathan (b. 6 Oct 1727), Mehitable (1728/9) and John (1730) ([R4-S1]). The list includes Daniel of Goshen (will 1761) and James Jr. of New Windsor (will 1756), whose wills fit. WikiTree gives her a death of 1738, unsourced. Her father Jonathan Browne is given on WikiTree as d. 19 Aug 1710 at Orient. The Salmon Record has a 'Jonathan Brown died' on 18 Sept, apparently 1704 by its sequence ([R4-S2]). This could be a different Jonathan Brown, but the conflict should be checked."
