   "bio": "Daniel Sayre lived at Southampton on Long Island. His will, dated 21 August 1707 and proved 13 April 1708, names his daughter Hannah as the wife of Josiah Topping and shows that she had no daughter Jerusha, which is why the Sayres are not among John's ancestors. The will has a humane touch: he asked that his enslaved woman 'may have Liberty to chuse her master when she is sold' and that she keep her clothes and her box.",
