   "bio": "Hannah Brewster was born on 19 May 1679, a daughter, most probably, of the Rev. Nathaniel Brewster; her family was not descended from the Mayflower Brewsters. She married first, at Brookhaven on 16 January 1703, John Muncy, who died on 12 June 1707, and second, at Setauket on 6 November 1709, Samuel Thompson. She was the mother of Susannah Thompson Strong and grandmother of Captain Selah Strong, so that Samuel's descendants carry both Thompson and Brewster blood. Hannah died on 7 November 1755 and was buried with Samuel at the south-east corner of the Setauket Presbyterian churchyard.\n\nShe was once shown as the wife of John Thompson and John's 10th-great-grandmother. Her marriage to Samuel Thompson instead makes that link probably wrong, and she is not counted as John's ancestor.",
