   "bio": "Jesse Woodhull was born on 10 February 1735 and died on 3 February 1795. During the American Revolution he commanded the 1st Regiment of Orange County Militia, the Cornwall-area regiment, and he later sat in the New York State Senate. Thomas Lamoreaux, John's 6th-great-grandfather, is recorded as having served under a \"Colonel Woodhull\", and that colonel was very probably Jesse, so Thomas most likely served under a cousin of his wife Keturah.\n\nJesse descended from Bull Smith of Smithtown through Richard Smith 2d and Sarah Smith, born 13 February 1700, who married Nathaniel Woodhull of Mastic in 1716. That makes him John's 2nd cousin nine times removed; a second, more doubtful line through the Topping family has also been suggested. His daughter Hannah, born 8 July 1761, married Oliver Smith of Moriches, another of Bull Smith's descendants.",
