   "bio": "William Floyd, born 17 December 1734, was a signer of the Declaration of Independence. His mother Tabitha Smith (1704-1755) was a daughter of Jonathan Smith 2d and Elizabeth Platt and a granddaughter of Bull Smith's eldest son Jonathan, who married Sarah Brewster; his father, Nicoll Floyd, died in March 1755 aged 50. That descent makes William John's 3rd cousin 8 times removed. He was once also counted a cousin through the Brewster line, but that connection has probably been disproved.\n\nHis sister Ruth married General Nathaniel Woodhull. His other siblings were Tabitha (Mrs Daniel Smith), Nicoll, Charles, Charity (Mrs Ezra L'Hommedieu), Mary (Mrs Edmund Smith), Catherine (Mrs Gen. Thomas Thomas) and Anna (Mrs Hugh Smith).",
