   "bio": "Rev. Nathaniel Brewster graduated in Harvard's first class in 1642. He was at Walberswick in Suffolk in 1649, served as minister of Alby and Thwaite in Norfolk, and in 1655 was sent by Cromwell to Ireland with Henry Cromwell. He later became the first minister of Brookhaven on Long Island. Sources disagree on whether he was born in America or at Bristol.\n\nHis wife was a daughter of Roger Ludlow, deputy-governor of Massachusetts and framer of Connecticut's code of laws; Ludlow is said to have removed to Virginia in 1654, though in fact he visited his brother George there and then went to Ireland. Their daughter Hannah married John Muncy and then Samuel Thompson. Brewster is not an ancestor of John, and his kinship to the family rests on the still unresolved question of the Brewster line.",
