   "researchNotes": "Path: Bull Smith → Richard 2d → Nathaniel (m. Phoebe Howell) → Mary (b. 3 Oct 1725, m. 12 June 1745 Col. Abraham Gardiner, b. 1721/2) → Capt. Abraham Gardiner (1763–1796, m. Phoebe Dayton) → David Gardiner (1784–1844) → Julia. Married President John Tyler in 1844; lived at Sherwood Forest Plantation, Charles City County, Virginia. With Anna Symmes Harrison, both First Ladies of the 1840 'Tippecanoe and Tyler Too' ticket are John's cousins; neither president is.\n\nEach generation now sourced in two independent compiled works (Gardiner 1890, [R4-S1]; Pelletreau 1898, [R4-S2]): Bull Smith -> Richard 2d -> Nathaniel Smith (b. 30 Jan 1698, d. 30 Mar 1765, patentee of Moriches) -> Mary (b. 3 Oct 1725, m. 12 Jun 1745 Col. Abraham Gardiner) -> Capt. Abraham Gardiner (1763-1796, m. Phoebe Dayton) -> Sen. David Gardiner (1784-1844) -> Julia: 5th cousin 6 times removed. Gardiner ([R4-S1]) lists her children with President Tyler as David G., John A., Julia, Lachlan, Lyon G., Robert Fitzwalter and Pearl."
