   "bio": "David Gardiner was born in May 1784; the records disagree on whether the day was the 2nd or the 29th. He was educated and made his career in New York and East Hampton between 1804 and 1828, married in New York in 1816, and served as a New York state senator. On 28 February 1844 he was aboard the USS Princeton on the Potomac River near Mount Vernon when the great 'Peacemaker' gun burst; he was one of the seven people killed. His widow's will was later contested and rejected by the Court of Appeals in what became known as 'a celebrated Will case'. Through Bull Smith he was John's 4th cousin 7 times removed.",
