   "bio": "Theodorus Bailey was born on 12 April 1805 and died on 10 February 1877. An officer of the US Navy, he rose to rear admiral and in the Civil War was Farragut's second-in-command at the capture of New Orleans in 1862.\n\nHe descended from Bull Smith of Smithtown through Richard Smith 2d and Richard Smith 3d, born 16 April 1696, whose daughter Phebe, born 19 August 1743, married Capt. Nathaniel Platt, a founder of Plattsburgh, on 10 November 1776. Their daughter Phebe Platt married Judge William Bailey of Plattsburgh and became the admiral's mother, which makes him John's 4th cousin 7 times removed. His wife, Sarah Ann Platt, was a cousin too, descending from Job Smith through Job 2d, Anna, Richard Smith 4th and Dorothy, who married Isaac S. Platt, so their children descended from Bull Smith by several lines. Richard Smith 3d's daughter Sarah, the admiral's great-aunt, married the Rev. Naphtali Daggett, later president of Yale.",
