   "summary": "Smithtown heir who died in the sinking of the Titanic in 1912, brother-in-law of the architect Stanford White; John's 5th cousin 5x removed.",
   "bio": "James Clinch Smith was born in 1856 at Smithtown, Long Island, the son of Judge J. Lawrence Smith, and inherited his father's homestead. Through his father's line he descends from Job Smith, John's own ancestor, by way of Job 2d, Anna, Richard 4th, Richard 5th and J. Lawrence Smith, which makes him John's 5th cousin five times removed; through Gen. Nathaniel Woodhull and Bull Smith he is also a 6th cousin five times removed.\n\nHe married the musician Bertha Ludington Barnes and lived in Paris. His sister Bessie married the architect Stanford White, and in 1906 James witnessed White's murder. Travelling first class on the Titanic, he died in the sinking on 15 April 1912; his body was not recovered.",
