   "researchNotes": "Path: John Thompson → Samuel → Jonathan → Dr. Samuel → Benjamin. Also 4C8R via Brewster (affected by the Brewster disproof) and probably 4C8R via Topping (his grandmother Mary Woodhull, b. 1711, appears to be a granddaughter of Temperance Topping). Called John Thompson 'the first Long Island ancestor of the compiler'.\n\nSon of Dr. Samuel Thompson and his first wife Phebe Satterly ([R4-S1]); 3rd cousin 8 times removed via John Thompson. Irony worth telling: his own family account (the source used by earlier rounds) contains the two errors later disproved, the 1609 birth and the Mayflower Brewster wife for John Thompson."
