   "bio": "John Franklin Farnsworth was born on 27 March 1820 at Eaton, Quebec, in Canada. In the Civil War he was colonel of the 8th Illinois Cavalry and was brevetted brigadier general, and he represented Illinois in Congress. He died on 14 July 1897.\n\nHis descent from the Hammonds of Watertown runs from William Hammond through Lt. John Hammond; his daughter Abigail, who married John Hastings; their son John Hastings; and his daughter Hannah Hastings, born at Watertown in 1716/17, who on 15 August 1735 married Lt. David Farnsworth, a settler of 'No. 4', Charlestown, New Hampshire, who was captured by the French and Indians in April 1757 and escaped after seventeen days. Their son Samuel Farnsworth, born in 1750, was a drummer at Bunker Hill and later lived in Canada; his son John, born at Stoddard, New Hampshire, on 15 May 1783, was a surveyor who died in Michigan in 1844 and was the Congressman's father. John F. Farnsworth is John's 6th cousin six times removed, and Samuel Farnsworth the drummer is his 4th cousin eight times removed.",
