   "researchNotes": "Path: Lt. John Hammond → Abigail (m. John Hastings) → John Hastings → Hannah (m. Lt. David Farnsworth, captured by Indians at No. 4 in 1757) → Samuel → John → John F. Samuel Farnsworth, drummer at Bunker Hill, is 4C8R.\n\nHammond ([R4-S1]) gives each generation: William Hammond (I) -> Lt. John Hammond (II) -> Abigail (III, m. John Hastings) -> John Hastings (IV) -> Hannah Hastings (V, b. Watertown 1716/17, m. 15 Aug 1735 Lt. David Farnsworth, a settler of 'No. 4' Charlestown, N.H., captured by the French and Indians in April 1757, escaped after seventeen days) -> Samuel Farnsworth (VI, b. 1750, drummer at Bunker Hill, later in Canada) -> John (VII, b. Stoddard, N.H., 15 May 1783, surveyor, d. Michigan 1844) -> John Franklin (VIII, b. 27 Mar 1820). 6th cousin 6 times removed."
