   "summary": "Founder of the Litchfield Law School and brother-in-law of Aaron Burr, born at Fire Place in Brookhaven; a possible Topping cousin of John.",
   "bio": "Tapping Reeve was born at Fire Place in Brookhaven, Long Island, on 1 October 1744 and died on 13 December 1823. He founded the Litchfield Law School and was a brother-in-law of Aaron Burr. His father, Rev. Abner Reeve, was born at Southold on 21 February 1707/8, a son of Thomas Reeve and Bethia Horton, and in December 1743 married Deborah Topping, or Tapping, of Brookhaven, who died in 1759 aged 42. Abner Reeve preached at Moriches from 1754 to 1763 and then removed with a company of emigrants from that neighbourhood to Blooming Grove in Orange County, New York, a movement that may also account for the Tuthill and Smith families' move.\n\nTapping Reeve's kinship to John is possible but unproven on two fronts: his mother's place in the Topping family has not been traced, and his grandmother Bethia Horton was surely of Barnabas Horton's Southold family, though which Bethia she was is not established.",
   "sources": [
    "F. B. Dexter, Biographical Sketches of the Graduates of Yale College vol. 1 pp. 434–5, https://archive.org/details/biogsketchgrad01dextuoft",
    "[R4-S1] F. B. Dexter, Biographical Sketches of the Graduates of Yale College, vol. 1 (1885) (archive.org full text), pp. 434-435 (secondary) https://archive.org/details/biogsketchgrad01dextuoft",
    "[R4-S2] Wikipedia, 'Tapping Reeve' (intro via MediaWiki API) (secondary) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tapping_Reeve",
    "[R4-S3] George F. Horton, Horton Genealogy, or Chronicles of the Descendants of Barnabas Horton (1876) (archive.org full text), c. p. 170 (Caleb I line) (secondary) https://archive.org/details/hortongenealogyo00hort"
   ],
