   "openQuestions": [
    "Which Bethia Horton married Thomas Reeve (b. 1671, d. 1738) as his first wife? The Horton Genealogy (1876) names a Bethia, daughter of Barnabas Horton (son of Caleb) and Sarah Hines of Cutchogue (m. c.1686), who would fit; that would make Tapping a Barnabas Horton descendant (4C8R via Barnabas, if the Rachel Browne -> Horton line holds).",
    "Deborah Topping (d. 1759, aged 42): her father is still unknown."
   ],
   "researchNotes": "Mother Deborah Topping/Tapping (m. Rev. Abner Reeve Dec 1743; d. 1759 aged 42). Rev. Abner Reeve preached at Moriches 1754–63 and in 1763 'removed with a company of emigrants from that neighborhood to Blooming Grove, Orange County' (Dexter vol. 1 pp. 434–5) — a possible vehicle for the Tuthill/Smith move.\n\nDexter ([R4-S1]) gives the family: his father Rev. Abner Reeve (b. Southold 21 Feb 1707/8, son of Thomas and Bethia (Horton) Reeve) married Deborah Topping 'or Tapping' of Brookhaven in December 1743, and Tapping was born at Fire Place, Brookhaven, in 1744. That opens a second possible route to John: his grandmother Bethia Horton was surely of Barnabas Horton's Southold family, but which Bethia is not proven (see openQuestionsNew). His mother's place in the Topping family is still untraced."
