   "researchNotes": "Not in the Ancestry tree; identified in Round 2. FS tree LCPG-XKM (14-17 sources): Francesco 'Frank' Giannetta/Genett, b. 2 May 1869 Bisaccia (AV), son of Savino Giannetta (b. 1842) and Angelamaria Fede; immigrated about 1906; naturalized in Scranton (1920/1923, Middle District Court); lived in Dunmore Ward 5 1910-30; died in Dunmore 1934. 1931 marriage license of his daughter: father Frank, a blacksmith born in Italy, living in Dunmore. Round 3 read his Declaration of Intention No. 16537, US District Court, Scranton, 12 Jul 1920, under the name 'Frank Gennetti': born 2 May 1869 'Bisiccio' [Bisaccia]; aged 50; laborer; of 133 Sand St, Dunmore (Mollie's 1931 address); sailed from Naples on the SS Italia, arriving New York c.15 Apr 1903 (FS profile says 1906); last foreign residence Bisaccia; wife Angelina born in Italy. Marriage, Bisaccia, 1 Aug 1896, Matrimoni 1896 act 18 (FS's '1886' is a typo; Round 2 had flagged 1886 as impossible since Angelica would have been about 12): groom 27, possidente, son of the living Savino and Angelamaria Fede; bride Angelica Ferrantino, 23, born Sant'Angelo dei Lombardi, resident in Bisaccia, foundling. paese.app counts 916 US arrivals from Bisaccia 1830-1912, peaking in 1906, the year FS says he came. Bisaccia is about 12 km from Guardia Lombardi.\n\nThe 1910 census confirms the 1896 Bisaccia marriage: Francesco 'Janet', 41, said he had been married 14 years. He was then a contractor's laborer at 134 Sand Street, Dunmore, still an alien, living with his wife, the four children born in Italy (Sam, Marianna/Mariano, Marie and Tony) and two Italian boarders ([R4-S2]). By January 1920 he owned the house at 133 Sand Street (with a mortgage) and worked as a laborer in the railroad shops. His sons Sam and Marion worked at a coal breaker, and the household had grown to seven children at home ([R4-S3]). In May 1933 he was still living at 133 Sand Street when son Joseph married at St. Rocco's, the Guardiese church in Dunmore ([R4-S4]). He died eleven months later. The state death index lists 'Francesco Giannett' of Dunmore, died 14 April 1934, file number 36353 ([R4-S1]). By 1940 his widow was head of the household ([R4-S5])."
