   "summary": "John's maternal 3rd great-grandfather, a shepherd of Bisaccia in Campania and father of Frank Giannetta.",
   "bio": "Savino Giannetta was born at Bisaccia in Avellino, Campania, Italy, on 12 January 1842, the son of Francesco Giannetta and, probably, Lucia Macchia. He was named after an elder brother Savino (1838–1841) who died in infancy and after his grandfather Savino Giannetta (about 1786–1853). He was John's maternal 3rd great-grandfather.\n\nHe was a pecoraio, or shepherd, as were the Fedes; both families followed the trade typical of the upland grazing country around Bisaccia. On 20 July 1867, aged 24 and with his father already dead, he married eighteen-year-old Angelamaria Fede at Bisaccia. Their children were Francesco 'Frank' (born 2 May 1869), Lucia (14 April 1872), Antonio (14 February 1874 – 3 November 1903), a second Lucia (19 February 1877 – 17 August 1878), Maria Giuseppa 'Josephine' (born 11 March 1880, later Mrs. Michele Ragazzo of Hartford, Connecticut), Nunzianda (about 1885 – 10 March 1888) and Bartolomeo (5–25 July 1889). The repeated names and early deaths reflect the high infant mortality of Bisaccia. Savino was still living when his son Frank married on 1 August 1896.",
