   "bio": "Francesco Maria Giannetta was born at Bisaccia, in Avellino, on 6 March 1812, the son of Savino Giannetta (about 1786–1853) and Giuseppa Sena (1790–1822). On 27 June 1836 he married Lucia Macchia, whose surname is an uncertain reading of the handwriting in the records. After Giuseppa's death the elder Savino had married, in 1823, the widow Grazia Maria Gallicchio, who was Lucia's mother; if the records are right, Francesco married his own stepsister. His children were Savino (1838–1841) and a second Savino, born in 1842.\n\nFamily records give his death as 16 February 1848, aged 35, when the younger Savino was six; he was certainly dead by 20 July 1867, when that son's marriage act at Bisaccia described him as the son of 'the late Francesco'. His grandson Frank was named Francesco after him.",
