   "summary": "Wife of Francesco Gabriele Fiorillo of San Mango, named as Carmine Fiorillo's mother at his death; placed as John's 5th-great-grandmother, though she was probably his aunt.",
   "bio": "Vittoria Marrelli, whose surname is also written Marrello and Morelli, died before 17 November 1860. She was named as the mother of Carmine Fiorillo in the record of his death at San Mango in 1860, and on that basis she is placed as John's 5th-great-grandmother. The records, however, show that she was the wife of Francesco Gabriele Fiorillo, not of Carmine's father Domenico: her sons Gabriele, who died in 1839 aged seven, Angelo (about 1824–1912) and Lorenzo (about 1835–1915) are all recorded as children of Francesco Fiorillo and Vittoria Marrello. Carmine's own marriage in 1840, made in his mother's lifetime, names her as Maria Marrelli, so the death record evidently substituted the aunt's name for the mother's. Vittoria was therefore very probably Carmine's aunt, and Maria Marrello his mother.",
