   "bio": "Katie Petrillo was born in Pennsylvania about 1897, a daughter of the Scranton grocer John Petriello and his wife Marie, and was John's great-grandaunt. In the 1910 census she appears as Katie, aged thirteen, the eldest of the six children in the household, all six of Marie's children then being alive: Katie, Peter, Frank, Joseph, Tony and Charlie.\n\nShe is very probably the same person as Grace Petrillo, who was born on 5 January 1897 and would have been thirteen in April 1910 yet is not otherwise listed; \"Katie\" may have been a mishearing of \"Gracie\". The 1920 census adds a puzzle, recording a twenty-three-year-old \"Chas\", a son working as a coal-mine labourer, who cannot be the younger Charles, then only thirteen; the entry may be a garbled record of the same child or of another son. If Katie was a separate daughter, she had died by 1935.",
