   "researchNotes": "Katie, 13, in the 1910 census at 1030 Ash St. Geni lists 'Katie \"Chas\"'; Round 2 says 'Chas' is a census misreading (Chas = Charles in 1920). Died before 1935.\n\nThe 1910 census lists 'Katie', a daughter aged 13, born in Pennsylvania ([R4-S1]). Marie is recorded as mother of 6 children, all 6 living, and exactly six children are listed: Katie, Peter, Frank, Joseph, Tony and Charlie. Grace Petrillo, born 5 Jan 1897, would have been 13 in April 1910, yet she does not appear unless she is 'Katie'. Grace's 1943 repatriation card confirms she was US-born on that date ([R4-S2]). Katie and Grace are therefore very probably the same girl ('Katie' perhaps a mishearing of 'Gracie'). In the 1920 census the 23-year-old at no. 1028 is recorded as 'Chas', son, male, a coal-mine laborer ([R4-S3]). That entry is unexplained, since Charles Thomas was only 13. It may be a garbled entry for the same child, or a separate son not otherwise recorded."
