   "researchNotes": "b. 5 Jan 1897; married Joseph DiBiasi (d. 1958); naturalized 29 Jun 1943 (index; reason unknown - possibly citizenship lost by marrying an alien, speculative); d. Mar 1973; buried at St. Mary of Mt Carmel, Dunmore. Peter's birth date 26 Jul 1897 conflicts (twin? dates conflict).\n\nGrace's 1943 'naturalization' was in fact a repatriation. The index card is marked 'Rep.' and gives her country of birth as the U.S.A. ([R4-S1]). Under the Expatriation Act of 1907, an American woman who married a foreigner took his nationality. Grace's husband Joseph DiBiasi was Italian-born, so she must have married him before the Cable Act took effect in September 1922, and she formally regained her citizenship in June 1943. In 1940 she and Joseph lived at 1015 Bunker Hill Street, where Grace, not Joseph, was the merchant running a general grocery store ([R4-S2]). She was carrying on the grocery trade of her father John Petriello, whose store had stood at 1028 on the same street. She is very probably the 'Katie', 13, of the 1910 census ([R4-S3]; see H0350)."
