   "summary": "Scranton-born homemaker who lived on Bunker Hill Street with her husband Nicholas Castellano and died in Phoenix, Arizona, at 91; John's great-grandaunt.",
   "bio": "Josephine Petrillo was born in Scranton, Pennsylvania, on 21 July 1904. She married Nicola, or Nicholas, Castellano, a railroad car repairer, and in 1940 the couple lived at 1003 Bunker Hill Street in Scranton, a few doors from her parents' old home, with their children Vito, Carmella and Marie.\n\nShe later moved to Phoenix, Arizona, where she died on 28 November 1995, aged 91. Her obituary described her as a homemaker and listed her survivors as her daughters Carmella Valvano and Marie Liburdi, her son Vito, her brothers Nick, Jim and Rocco Petrillo, nine grandchildren and fifteen great-grandchildren. Her funeral Mass was said at St. Theresa Catholic Church in Phoenix.",
