   "researchNotes": "Geni: Rocco James b. 8 Sep 1889, Italy (Round 2 FS: 19 Sep 1889). Immigrated 1909; lived in Farrell and Berwick, PA and in Ohio; died 1980. His removal voids Round 1's 'first arrival 1889-95' inference for John Petriello.\n\nRocco James Petrello's 1942 'old man's' draft registration gives his birth as 8 Sept 1889 in Italy. That matches Geni's 8 Sep 1889 rather than the FamilySearch tree's 19 Sep ([R4-S1]). He was then living at 337 North Bromley Avenue in Scranton's West Side with his wife Mary (Giordano), and worked for American Car & Foundry at Berwick. So this other Guardiese Petriello family also passed through Scranton, but there is still no evidence linking him to John Petriello's household. He is the son of Michelarcangelo Petriello and Benedetta Ladye (FS) and should not be merged with John's children."
