   "bio": "Charity Gould was born on 16 February 1800 in Salem Township, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, the eldest child of Jacob Gould and Hannah Davenport. Her father, a New Jersey soldier of the Revolution, died in 1849 aged 77 and was buried in the old Shupp cemetery at Plymouth; her mother was a daughter of Thomas and Charity (Lamoreux) Davenport.\n\nAbout 1821 she married Benjamin Pringle (1794–1853), son of Samuel and Martha (Lamoreaux) Pringle, which made her at once a granddaughter of Charity Lamoreux Davenport and a daughter-in-law of Martha Lamoreaux Pringle. Their children were Bethia, who married Caleb Roberts in 1852 and went to Iowa, dying a widow at Verona, Faribault County, Minnesota, on 30 December 1897; Martha Ann, who married William Hutchinson; Elijah, called Lege (about 1825–1898), who died in Salem Township; Ira (about 1834–1918); Jacob Gould; Martin, who went to California; and Caleb, born in 1839, who \"went West\".\n\nThe family lived in Salem Township from 1860 to 1880. According to family records Charity died in Lehman Township on 19 January 1883 and was buried in Beach Grove Cemetery at Beach Haven.",
