   "bio": "Francis J. Randall, whose name also appears as Randell and Randel, was born in Pennsylvania about 1846. In the Civil War he served as a private in the 2nd Battery, Connecticut Volunteer Light Artillery, enlisting on 23 February 1864 and receiving his discharge on 9 August 1865. About 1868 he married Sarah E. VanDuzen (1849–1876), and their daughter Katherine May was born at Plymouth on 24 April 1869. In 1870 he was living in Lackawanna Township.\n\nWidowed in 1876, he married Ellen Jane Pringle, the daughter of Andrew G. Pringle and Catherine Scott, at Plymouth on 14 December 1876, when she was only 14. Their children were Frederick (1878–1931) and Gertrude Helen (1882–1956). He was living at Plymouth in 1880 and died there on 15 November 1890, after which Ellen drew a widow's pension for his war service. She survived him by many years and died at Wilkes-Barre on 12 March 1938.",
