   "bio": "Mathias Van Loon came to Plymouth, Luzerne Co., PA, from Esopus in Ulster County, New York, in 1794, one of three brothers of Low Dutch origin, Abraham (known as Brom), Mathias and Nicholas, all of whom appear on the Plymouth assessment list of 1796. A local historian remembered them as \"a family of hard workers\". Mathias is counted with Thomas Lamoreaux among the earliest settlers of Jackson Township, the hill country west of Shawnee mountain where the Lamoreaux family settled.\n\nHe married Temperance Lamoreaux (1778–1855), daughter of Ensign Thomas Lamoreaux, and they had eight children. His nephew Stephen Van Loon, Abraham's eldest son, married Temperance's sister Hannah, so that uncle and nephew were married to two sisters.",
