   "bio": "Suzanne Marie Doucinet came from La Rochelle in France. On Sunday 6 August 1693 she married Daniel Mercereau, of Moëze in Saintonge, at the French Church of New York. Among the witnesses who marked the register were 'the sieur Doucinet', probably Estienne Dousinet, a New York shoemaker who appears elsewhere in the same register as a sponsor, and Elisabet Dubois, the groom's mother. Earlier that summer, on 25 June 1693, Suzanne had stood as godmother, with Jean La Tourette, to Pierre, son of Pierre Masse and Elisabet Mercereau; she could sign only with her mark.\n\nHer children with Daniel were Daniel, born on 10 August 1695 and baptized eight days later with Pierre Masse and Judy Pare as sponsors; Susanne Marie, born on 8 July 1697; and Marianne, born on 31 October 1699, whose sponsors were Joshue Mercereau and Jeanne Jamain.",
