   "bio": "Elizabeth Sorber was the youngest named child of Abraham Sorber, a man \"of German descent\" who came from Northampton County to Hanover Township in Luzerne County about 1783 with a family of grown children, so she was probably born in Northampton County. Her brothers were John, who married Betsey Sleppy and moved to Butler Township, George (1778–1860), who married Elizabeth Ehra, Jacob, who married a Cease, and Henry, who also went to Butler Township.\n\nElizabeth married John Croop. The Croops came to Hunlock's Creek with \"the numerous family of Sorbers\", and the two families built the sawmills there; John Croop held 200 acres in what is now Hunlock Township and raised ten children. His son William Croop, born in Newport Township, married Mary Sorber of Northampton County, and their son Hiram Croop, born in 1832, is described as a grandson of both John Croop and Philip Sorber, a son of Jacob. If Elizabeth was William's mother, William married a Sorber cousin.",
