   "bio": "Jacob Sorber is said to have married Maria Engel Doll, who was born at Ulmet in 1717, in 1739, and to have been the father of Abraham Sorber, born in 1744, who brought his family from Northampton County to Hanover Township in Luzerne County about 1783. The marriage rests on family trees rather than on a surviving record.\n\nOne possible origin is the party of Sorbers, or Servers, who arrived at Philadelphia on the ship Elizabeth and qualified there on 27 August 1733. It included a Jacob aged 56, a Jacob Jr. aged 36 and a Rudolph aged 21. Jacob Jr., born about 1697, would have been about 42 at a marriage in 1739 to a bride of 22, which is possible as a second marriage; the elder Jacob is too old to fit, and there may have been another Jacob altogether.\n\nHe should not be confused with the later Jacob Sorber, Abraham's son, who married a Cease and settled in Plymouth Township in 1827 with Henry Cease and George Sorber; that Jacob, or yet another, was the father of the Philip Sorber who settled up Hunlock's Creek.",
