   "bio": "Joseph DiBiasi was born in Italy on 18 April 1891 and died at Scranton, Lackawanna County, PA, on 31 May 1958. He was still an Italian subject when he married Grace Petrillo, some time before September 1922, but by 1940 he had become a naturalized citizen and owned the house at 1015 Bunker Hill Street in Scranton, where Grace kept a general grocery; James DiBiasi, 45, also Italian-born, owned the other half of the same building. Joseph's parents are unknown. The suggestion that he was a son of Giovanni Pasquale DiBiasi and Rosa Siconolfi is impossible on Rosa's age, and would have made Grace his niece; a widowed Vincenzo DiBiasi, born about 1866, who lived a few doors away on Bunker Hill Street in 1940, is a possible father.",
